30-2f93e19de326'}, {'abstract': 'Few artists have been so identified with one small patch of terrain as Mr. Christenberry, who used Hale County, Ala., as the inspiration for many of his works.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/arts/design/william-christenberry-dead.html', 'snippet': 'Few artists have been so identified with one small patch of terrain as Mr. Christenberry, who used Hale County, Ala., as the inspiration for many of his works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'William A. Christenberry, whose widely admired color photographs of the red-clay landscapes and kudzu-wreathed dwellings in his native corner of the rural South describe the slow passage of time there with plain-spoken eloquence, died on Monday in Washington. He was 80.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'William A. Christenberry, Photographer of Rural South, Dies at 80', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'William A. Christenberry Dies at 80; Photographed the Rural Deep South', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woodward, Richard B', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christenberry, William A (1936-2016)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-01T02:40:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard B. Woodward', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/94e1e1f3-3234-5b15-81a2-b0bc94acbd15', 'word