', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/arts/01CYCLONESUB/01CYCLONESUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/01/arts/01CYCLONESUB/01CYCLONESUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/arts/01CYCLONESUB/01CYCLONESUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Teenagers Sing to Survive in ‘Ride the Cyclone’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Teenagers Singing to Survive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Ride the Cyclone (Play)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lortel, Lucille, Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maxwell, Brooke', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richmond, Jacob', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rockwell, Rachel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MCC Theater', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-01T03:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1b68b56-a6a4-5764-b7f6-98e3fb70b991', 'word_count': 929, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1b68b56-a6a4-5764-b7f6-98e3fb70b991'}, {'abstract': 'It’s hard to have a bad episode with Cookie Lyon at the center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/arts/television/empire-season-3-episode-7-queen-cookie.html', 'snippet': 'It’s hard to have a bad episode with Cookie Lyon at the center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You might want to sit down before you read this oh-so-shocking revelation: When “Empire” put Cookie Lyon at the center of an episode, it got the best episode of its third season so far. Largely pushing Lucious and the constant conflicts he engenders between his sons to the side, this week’s focus was squarely on the queen as she attempted to bring her scatterbrained family together to impress the family of her once-again boyfriend, the New York City mayoral candidate Angelo DuBois. Taraji P. Henson’s unerring ability to find the core of Cookie’s every interaction and mine it for all it’s worth is the show’s greatest renewable resource.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/watching/30empire/empire-watching-recommendation-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/30/watching/30empire/empire-watching-recommendation-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/watching/30empire/empire-watching-recommendation-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/30/watching/30empire/empire-watching-recommendation-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/30/watching/30empire/empire-watching-recommendation-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': No