izations', 'value': 'Revolutionary Armed Forces of Colombia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santos, Juan Manuel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-01T03:12:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Casey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Casey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/410a92b2-2af5-5204-b13e-0c13530b731e', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/410a92b2-2af5-5204-b13e-0c13530b731e'}, {'abstract': 'This time, the Mets’ courtship of Yoenis Cespedes was different. It was mutual and featured a lot of communication.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/sports/baseball/yoenis-cespedes-new-york-mets.html', 'snippet': 'This time, the Mets’ courtship of Yoenis Cespedes was different. It was mutual and featured a lot of communication.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This time, the Mets’ courtship of Yoenis Cespedes was different. It was mutual. Cespedes, the star outfielder, was not out of work in late January and still negotiating with teams, as he was last winter. From the start of this off-season — in fact, even before it — the Mets and Cespedes knew they wanted to stay together.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/sports/01-CITY-METS/01-CITY-METS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/01/sports/01-CITY-METS/01-CITY-METS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlar