tic Republic of (Congo-Kinshasa)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Syrian American Medical Society', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fonkoze', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Equal Justice Initiative', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deng, Valentino Achak', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-01T08:21:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/125a6ef8-dc4e-57e7-850f-dc014632d6f9', 'word_count': 815, 'uri': 'nyt://article/125a6ef8-dc4e-57e7-850f-dc014632d6f9'}, {'abstract': 'Threats and self-dealing don’t get a negotiator very far in Havana.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/01/opinion/what-trump-misses-about-cuba.html', 'snippet': 'Threats and self-dealing don’t get a negotiator very far in Havana.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — DONALD J. TRUMP has never felt compelled to play by conventional rules — neither in business nor in politics — and that iconoclasm has made him a billionaire and president-elect of the United States. But if he thinks he can use his business practices abroad as a model for negotiations with foreign governments, he will be in for a rude awakening, especially with Cuba. Mr. Trump’s foreign business deals have been lucrative, but they exemplify just the sort of cronyism and shady dealing that characterized American business practices in Cuba before Fidel Castro’s revolution — practices that stoked Cuban nationalism, increased Mr. Castro’s popularity and led to the seizure of over a billion dollars of American property.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/opinion/01leograndeWeb/01leograndeWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 528, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/01/opinion/01leograndeWeb/01leograndeWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 528}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/opinion/01leograndeWeb/01leograndeWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 902, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/opinion/01leograndeWeb/01leograndeWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1804, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/opinion/01leograndeWeb/01leograndeWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/01/opinion/01leograndeWeb/01leograndeWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/opinion/01leograndeWeb/01leograndeWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Trump Misses About Cuba', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Trump Misses About Cuba', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LeoGrande, William M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castro, Fidel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-01T08:21:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By William M. Leogrande', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7f04f23-5dc7-57ce-a0fa-b7b926349c1e', 'word_count': 889, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7f04f23-5dc7-57ce-a0fa-b7b926349c1e'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Trump, who has offered only a jumble of contradictory ideas, will have a hard time dealing with urgent challenges abroad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/01/opinion/a-world-of-trouble-for-donald-trump.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Trump, who has offered only a jumble of contradictory ideas, will have a hard time dealing with urgent challenges abroad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That Donald Trump is having trouble choosing a secretary of state underscores concerns about his ability to manage the international challenges he will face in office — from the aggression of leaders like Russia’s Vladimir Putin to the Islamic State to strains among NATO allies.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/opinion/1thu1/1thu1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'