', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Series', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-01T08:21:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/641fac35-5102-5435-b394-fd413b433b49', 'word_count': 909, 'uri': 'nyt://article/641fac35-5102-5435-b394-fd413b433b49'}, {'abstract': 'Donald Trump’s nomination of Seema Verma suggests states will be given more power to remodel their Medicaid programs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/01/upshot/a-trump-pick-and-why-indianas-strict-medicaid-rules-could-spread.html', 'snippet': 'Donald Trump’s nomination of Seema Verma suggests states will be given more power to remodel their Medicaid programs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In most of the United States, anyone poor enough to qualify for Medicaid simply receives whatever care doctors recommend at minimal cost. But many Medicaid enrollees in Indiana can’t get full benefits unless they pay monthly premiums, and some who fail to pay can be shut out of coverage entirely for six months. If they go to the emergency room too often, they have to pay a fee.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/upshot/01UP-medicare/01UP-CMS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/01/upshot/01UP-medicare/01UP-CMS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbna