 {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indiana', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-01T08:30:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margot Sanger-Katz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margot', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanger-Katz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/577da13b-909f-5068-9d4c-4af4552a16f6', 'word_count': 938, 'uri': 'nyt://article/577da13b-909f-5068-9d4c-4af4552a16f6'}, {'abstract': 'An Alaska Native turns to the fashion world to send a message about hunting, history and haute couture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/01/fashion/sea-otter-fur-hunting-alaska-fashion-debate.html', 'snippet': 'An Alaska Native turns to the fashion world to send a message about hunting, history and haute couture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recently a giant billboard went up in Midtown Manhattan. It is 29 feet high and 13 feet wide, and shows a naked Alicia Silverstone in a grassy field peeking coyly over her shoulder and holding a sheep’s mask. The message: “I’d rather go naked than wear wool: Wear your own skin. Let animals keep theirs.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/fashion/UNBUTTONED/UNBUTTONED-WEB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/01/fashion/UNBUTTONED/UNBUTTONED-WEB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/fashion/UNBUTTONED/UNBUTTONED-WEB1-jumbo.jpg', 'height'