'', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccde5100-20cc-54db-89e1-ddeed4c65f44', 'word_count': 841, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccde5100-20cc-54db-89e1-ddeed4c65f44'}, {'abstract': 'The Russian leader lamented rising global “fractures,” even in affluent countries, but made no mention of the Kremlin’s efforts to stir up disorder.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/01/world/europe/vladimir-putin-us-russia.html', 'snippet': 'The Russian leader lamented rising global “fractures,” even in affluent countries, but made no mention of the Kremlin’s efforts to stir up disorder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — After the outpouring of euphoria among Russia’s political elite over the victory of Donald J. Trump, President Vladimir V. Putin on Thursday gave a more measured response in his annual address to the nation, calling for cooperation but expressing misgivings over some of Mr. Trump’s statements about nuclear weapons.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Subdued Vladimir Putin Calls for ‘Mutually Beneficial’ Ties With U.S.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Measured Speech, Putin Calls for ‘Mutually Beneficial’ Ties With U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Higgins, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-01T16:54:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Higgins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Higgins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36696d6c-4eb1-5f45-beb7-7f2dcdf0e247', 'word_count': 1156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36696d6c-4eb1-5f45-beb7-7f2dcdf0e247'}, {'abstract': 'Benjamin Millepied stages “Homecoming” at the Ace Hotel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/01/t-magazine/entertainment/benjamin-millepied-ballet-homecoming-los-angeles.html', 'snippet': 'Benjamin Millepied stages “Homecoming” at the Ace Hotel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It seems fitting that the world premiere of “Homecoming,” a new ballet from Benjamin Millepied, will take place in Los Angeles, where he recently returned after a stint leading the Paris Opera Ballet. But don’t expect an on-the-nose celebration. The piece is an abstract duet set to songs by Rufus Wainwright, who will live-accompany Millepied and Janie Taylor, a new addition to Millepied’s company, L.A. Dance Project. If anything, says the choreographer, it’s about a couple “losing and finding each other within a relationship.” It’s also inherently about the idea of what ballet can be. “Dance is really the art that assembles other art,” he says. For “On the Other Side” — making its U.S. premiere alongside “Homecoming” at the gorgeously restored Art Deco theater at the Ace Hotel in downtown Los Angeles — Millepied enlisted the painter Mark Bradford to design the sets.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '68', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/t-magazine/ballet-millepied/ballet-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/02/t-magazine/ballet-millepied/ballet-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/t-magazine/ballet-millepied/ballet-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/t-magazine/ballet-millepied/ballet-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/02/t-magazine/ballet-millepied/ballet-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/t-magazine/ballet-millepied/ballet-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/t-magazine/ballet-millepied/ballet-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Art-Filled Ballet Comes to Los Angeles', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dancing With the Stars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LA Dance Project', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ace Hotel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Millepied, Benjamin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-01T16:55:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 