major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-01T17:24:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/71abe936-a592-5214-ab05-9282b5b02562', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71abe936-a592-5214-ab05-9282b5b02562'}, {'abstract': 'The prince was crowned as King Maha Vajiralongkorn Bodindradebayavarangkun seven weeks after the death of his father, a revered figure in Thailand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/01/world/asia/thailand-king.html', 'snippet': 'The prince was crowned as King Maha Vajiralongkorn Bodindradebayavarangkun seven weeks after the death of his father, a revered figure in Thailand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGKOK — Thailand’s crown prince ascended to the throne on Thursday, seven weeks after the death of his father, King Bhumibol Adulyadej, who died after reigning for seven decades.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New King for Thailand as Crown Prince, Vajiralongkorn, Ascends to Throne', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vajiralongkorn (1952- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bhumibol Adulyadej', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Families', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-01T17:38:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard C. Paddock', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Paddock', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/481e5304-e1ea-553d-9dae-06fcce214131', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/481e5304-e1ea-553d-9dae-06fcce214131'}, {'abstract': 'From the omnipresent aroma of palo santo to a growing faith in Tarot, a new age vibe pulsed through the year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/01/t-magazine/practical-magic.html', 'snippet': 'From the omnipresent aroma of palo santo to a growing faith in Tarot, a new age vibe pulsed through the year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Palo santo, which means “holy stick” in Spanish, is a tree indigenous to the Caribbean and South America. When burned, it emits a fragrance of pine and citrus. Lighting a stick of palo santo, like burning a bundle of sage or sweetgrass, is believed to chase away misfortune. Amazonian shamans use it in ayahuasca ceremonies to cleanse a ceremonial space of bad spirits. Given its mystical connotations, it’s not a scent associated with the secular world, but lately I have noticed its distinctive smoke wafting over more earthly settings, from Brooklyn dive bars to blue-chip art openings.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '63', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/t-magazine/04tmag-13look_sign-t_CA0/04tmag-13look_sign-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/04/t-magazine/04tmag-13look_sign-t_CA0/04tmag-13look_sign-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/t-magazine/04tmag-13look_sign-t_CA0/04tmag-13look_sign-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/t-magazine/04tmag-13look_sign-t_CA0/04tmag-13look_sign-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/04/t-magazine/04tmag-13look_sign-t_CA0/04tmag-13look_sign-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 725}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/t-magazine/04tmag-13look_sign-t_CA0/04tmag-13look_sign-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 848, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/t-magazine/04tmag-13look_sign-t_CA0/04tmag-13look_sign-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1696, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Modern Charm of Practical Magic', 'kicker': 'Sign of the Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Year of Magical Thinking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Superstitions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magic and Magicians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-01T17:38:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Witt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea818e96-6f4d-5052-a40d-5902ea660496', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea818e96-6f4d-5052-a40d-5902ea660496'}, {'abstract': 'Miguel Zugaza will go back to the museum he led before the Prado; neither Spain’s culture ministry nor the Prado’s board indicated who might succeed him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/01/arts/design/miguel-zugaza-prado-museum-leave-for-bilbao.html', 'snippet': 'Miguel Zugaza will go back to the museum he led before the Prado; neither Spain’s culture ministry nor the Prado’s board indicated who might succeed him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — The director of the Prado museum, Miguel Zugaza, will step down early next year to return to the museum in Bilbao that he led before taking charge of the Prado in 2002.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/arts/02PRADO/02PRADO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/02/arts/02PRADO/02PRADO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/arts/02PRADO/02PRADO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/arts/02PRADO/02PRADO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1399, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/arts/02PRADO/02PRADO-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/02/arts/02PRADO/02PRADO-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/arts/02PRADO/02PRADO-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Prado Museum Director to Step Down and Return to Bilbao', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Director of the Prado Is Going Back Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Prado Museum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zugaza, Miguel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Madrid (Spain)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bilbao (Spain)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-01T17:39:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d350f0f3-f57c-5594-9326-261fe763fd77', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d350f0f3-f57c-5594-9326-261fe763fd77'}, {'abstract': 'Whatever Pope Francis wants, the church’s liberal wing is implementing a revolution.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/12/01/the-end-of-catholic-marriage/', 'snippet': 'Whatever Pope Francis wants, the church’s liberal wing is implementing a revolution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I haven’t written in this space for some time, but now that the election is over some additional interventions seem necessary to capture what’s happening in Roman Catholicism’s remarkable period of controversy. My Sunday column\xa0talked a bit about the way in which varying interpretations of “Amoris Laetitia,” Pope Francis’s apostolic exhortation on the family, have produced variations in official Catholic teaching on marriage from diocese to diocese, region to region – a “submerged schism,” to borrow a phrase from the Vatican-watcher Andrea Gagliarducci, which\xa0thanks to the astringent words of certain bishops is no longer even that submerged.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The End of Catholic Marriage', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'John Paul II', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-01T17:46:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/267662be-584e-557b-a8d2-f14584b0b25f', 'word_count': 2643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/267662be-584e-557b-a8d2-f14584b0b25f'}, {'abstract': 'The Spanish police said they had arrested 34 people suspected of being involved in fixing matches of low-level men’s players in Spain and Portugal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/01/sports/tennis/match-fixing-arrests-spain.html', 'snippet': 'The Spanish police said they had arrested 34 people suspected of being involved in fixing matches of low-level men’s players in Spain and Portugal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — The Spanish police arrested 34 people suspected of being involved in a criminal betting organization that fixed tennis matches in tournaments held in Spain and Portugal.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arrests Made in Spain After Tennis Match-Fixing Inquiry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '6 Tennis Players Arrested in Fixing Inquiry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tennis Integrity Unit', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-01T17:51:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b99de6c-170e-5470-ba74-541943644972', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b99de6c-170e-5470-ba74-541943644972'}, {'abstract': 'A reader says liberals, too, are guilty of “using the state to tell others how to live.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/01/opinion/liberals-and-soda-taxes.html', 'snippet': 'A reader says liberals, too, are guilty of “using the state to tell others how to live.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Liberals and Soda Taxes', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Liberals and Soda Taxes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soft Drinks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales and Excise Taxes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-01T17:54:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/a996783e-d46c-589a-ac03-8d9b22db5141', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a996783e-d46c-589a-ac03-8d9b22db5141'}, {'abstract': 'In the Upper Engadin, a 35-mile swath of the southeastern Swiss Alps, a crop of galleries have emerged as an après-ski alternative.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/01/t-magazine/art/engadin-switzerland-alps-art.html', 'snippet': 'In the Upper Engadin, a 35-mile swath of the southeastern Swiss Alps, a crop of galleries have emerged as an après-ski alternative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the curator and art dealer Vito Schnabel decided to open his first permanent gallery space last December, he chose St. Moritz over the art districts of Chai Wan, Chelsea or Wynwood. He’s not alone: Exhibitions in ski resorts have become something of a phenomenon lately. This past summer, the curator Neville Wakefield organized a group show featuring work by Dan Colen, Damien Hirst and Richard Prince in an Aspen ski shop, while in Gstaad, Hauser & Wirth erected an exhibition of monumental Calder sculptures (“Calder in the Alps,” on view through March 31, 2017), many of which had never been exhibited in Switzerland before.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/t-magazine/art/01tmag-altitude-slide-330M/01tmag-altitude-slide-330M-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/01/t-magazine/art/01tmag-altitude-slide-330M/0