b40a-52ba-924f-a992d3152b46'}, {'abstract': 'Glossy new books devoted to the lavish retreats of American “country house” living.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/01/books/review/country-living-our-time-at-foxhollow-farm-david-byars.html', 'snippet': 'Glossy new books devoted to the lavish retreats of American “country house” living.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Julian Fellowes may be adapting the “Downton Abbey” formula to a stateside setting, but why wait for his late-19th-century period piece, “The Gilded Age,” when you can escape right now into the well-apportioned drawing rooms of the past? Just crack open one of the glossy new books devoted to American “country house” living and concoct your own melodrama about the privileged few. The impulse behind their lavish retreats was to “get away from it all” — but, of course, the “all” often came right along with them.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/books/review/04Becker01-SUB/04Becker01-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/04/books/review/04Becker01-SUB/04Becker01-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/books/review/04Becker01-SUB/04Becker01-SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/books/review/04Becker01-SUB/04Becker01-SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1286, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12