ili, Ben Ziane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Casablanca (Morocco)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-01T21:01:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lorenzo Tondo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lorenzo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tondo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/848061e7-dbe2-54f2-a2c6-4958308967e6', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/848061e7-dbe2-54f2-a2c6-4958308967e6'}, {'abstract': 'Chef Rocky Barnette debuts a preconquest menu at the Capri this month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/01/t-magazine/food/capri-restaurant-marfa-rocky-barnette.html', 'snippet': 'Chef Rocky Barnette debuts a preconquest menu at the Capri this month.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Every mesquite tree tastes different, so you have to walk around tasting them all,” says chef Rocky Barnette about the southwestern plant that grows plentifully in Marfa, Tex., where he lives and cooks. The indigenous flora and fauna of the sleepy town have become an obsession for Barnette. So much so that in December, he will launch a preconquest tasting menu — a collection of dishes inspired by the ancient cuisines of the region — at the Capri, the restaurant and events space owned by his wife, the arts and culture philanthropist Virginia Lebermann.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/01/t-magazine/food/01tmag-capri-slide-NAM7/01tmag-capri-slide-NAM7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandar