k Times. I tried to shed light on the origins of luxuries created by members of oppressed communities, and the wanderings of belongings of persecuted families driven into exile. I set out to explain why we make what we make and why we buy what we buy, and asked what our possessions express about us, and about the extremes of human folly, greed, experimentation and ambition.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/arts/02ANTIQUES1/02ANTIQUES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/02/arts/02ANTIQUES1/02ANTIQUES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/arts/02ANTIQUES1/02ANTIQUES1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/arts/02ANTIQUES1/02ANTIQUES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/02/arts/02ANTIQUES1/02ANTIQUES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/arts/02ANTIQUES1/02ANTIQUES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 501, 'width': 750, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/arts/02ANTIQUES1/02ANTIQUES1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 501, 'width': 750, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Magnificent Obsessions: Pursuits of a Lifetime', 'kicker': 'Antiques', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Magnificent Obsessions: Pursuits of a Lifetime', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Memorabilia and Souvenirs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japanese-Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Alexander', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIQUES', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-01T21:49:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eve M. Kahn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46236fda-33f7-5334-9a2a-f4d180ddf35f', 'word_count': 969, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46236fda-33f7-5334-9a2a-f4d180ddf35f'}, {'abstract': 'Dito Montiel’s film, which stars Shia LaBeouf as a scarred veteran, imparts the urgency of its issue more effectively with statistics than with its script.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/01/movies/man-down-review-shia-labeouf.html', 'snippet': 'Dito Montiel’s film, which stars Shia LaBeouf as a scarred veteran, imparts the urgency of its issue more effectively with statistics than with its script.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early in “Man Down,” Gabriel, a battle-scarred Marine played by Shia LaBeouf, walks past a burned-out former factory building that’s spray-painted with the message “America We Have a Problem.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None,