es.com/2016/12/01/nyregion/jessica-lappin-sunday-routine.html', 'snippet': 'Aside from her run in Central Park, Ms. Lappin, the president of the Alliance for Downtown New York, spends most of her time with her husband and sons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jessica Lappin, president of the Alliance for Downtown New York, among the city’s largest business improvement districts, has a long history with Lower Manhattan. While she now calls a two-bedroom co-op in Midtown East home, in 1993 she was in the first graduating class of Stuyvesant High School’s Lower Manhattan campus. “Lower Manhattan was a ghost town on nights and weekends,” she said of the early 1990s. Since then, it has become one of the fastest-growing neighborhoods in the city. Ms. Lappin, 41, lives with her husband, Andrew Wuertele, 42, the chief administrative officer at East River Medical Imaging, and their sons, Lucas, 9, and Miles, 5.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/nyregion/04ROUTINE2/04ROUTINE2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 469, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/04/nyregion/04ROUTINE2/04ROUTINE2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 469}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/nyregion/04ROUTINE2/04ROUTINE2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 801, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/nyregion/04ROUTINE2/04ROUTINE2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1602, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/nyregion/04ROUTINE2/04ROUTINE2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/04/nyregion/04ROUTINE2/04ROUTINE2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/nyregion/04ROUTINE2/04ROUTINE2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Jessica Lappin, an Advocate for Lower Manhattan, Spends Her Sundays', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Downtown Maven, Midtown Mama', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ALLIANCE FOR DOWNTOWN NEW YORK', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Financial District (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-02T01:55:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Satow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Satow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e24166df-f474-5043-8857-56fc387bd9e7', 'word_count': 771, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e24166df-f474-5043-8857-56fc387bd9e7'}, {'abstract': 'The event resurrected signature applause lines and carried the hallmarks of Mr. Trump’s whiplash style during the election: indicting and promising, nostalgic and forward-looking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/01/us/politics/trump-kicks-off-thank-you-tour-reveling-in-crowd-and-campaign-themes.html', 'snippet': 'The event resurrected signature applause lines and carried the hallmarks of Mr. Trump’s whiplash style during the election: indicting and promising, nostalgic and forward-looking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CINCINNATI — He boasted about himself in the third person. He sneered at the opponents he had vanquished. He disparaged journalists and invited angry chants from the crowd, grinning broadly at calls of “lock her up” and “build the wall.” He ridiculed the government’s leaders as stupid and dishonest failures.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Kicks Off ‘Thank You’ Tour, Reveling in Crowd and Campaign Themes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boasts, Jeers and Some Jabs  as Trump Opens Victory Tour', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corasaniti, Nick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-02T02:01:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti and Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/163ca844-b9df-585a-997e-568751f27888', 'word_count': 1250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/163ca844-b9df-585a-997e-568751f27888'}, {'abstract': 'Catering to beauty professionals, Alcone Company, in Hell’s Kitchen, sells