mon remix.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/02/arts/music/playlist-burial-laura-marling-lil-yachty.html', 'snippet': 'Hear the new music that caught our pop critics’ attention this week, from Lil Yachty’s Beats 1 Freestyle to an imaginative Paul Simon remix.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every Friday, pop critics for The New York Times weigh in on the week’s most notable new songs and videos — and anything else that strikes them as intriguing. You can listen to this playlist on Spotify here. Like this Playlist? Let us know at theplaylist@nytimes.com, and sign up for our Louder newsletter (coming soon!) here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/03/arts/03playlist/03playlist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/03/arts/03playlist/03playlist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/03/arts/03playlist/03playlist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/03/arts/03playlist/03playlist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/03/arts/03playlist/03playlist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/03/arts/03playlist/03playlist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/03/arts/03playlist/03playlist-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Playlist: Burial and Laura Marling Slip Deeper Into the Void', 'kicker': 'Playlist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Erimaj', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'xx, The (Music Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bynum, Taylor Ho', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-02T17:16:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles, Jon Caramanica and Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48dd25b2-b0fc-5e0a-8c5f-ec0affbd1909', 'word_count': 1340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48dd25b2-b0fc-5e0a-8c5f-ec0affbd1909'}, {'abstract': 'It’s a big city, with plenty to do, see, hear and watch. Here’s a sampling of cultural highlights this weekend and over the week ahead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/02/arts/things-to-do-in-nyc-nutcracker-museum-of-sex.html', 'snippet': 'It’s a big city, with plenty to do, see, hear and watch. Here’s a sampling of cultural highlights this weekend and over the week ahead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Other Israel Film Festival — continuing through Thursday — emphasizes movies that focus on the country’s Arab and Palestinian communities. The selections include Udi Aloni’s “Junction 48” (Saturday), which won the best international narrative feature prize at this year’s Tribeca Film Festival; it follows a rapper (the real-life musician Tamer Nafar) and his girlfriend (Samar Qupty) as they channel their love of hip-hop into social protest. “Mr. Aloni fuses joy and sorrow throughout the film and ends with a devastating image encapsulating the intransigent forces that conspire to silence young artists,” Mike Hale wrote in The New York Times when the movie showed at Tribeca. Mr. Nafar will appear in concert with Marcus Mumford on Monday, at Le Poisson Rouge. BEN KENIGSBERG', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/arts/02LISTINGSMOVIES/02LISTINGSMOVIES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/02/arts/02LISTINGSMOVIES/02LISTINGSMOVIES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/arts/02LISTINGSMOVIES/02LISTINGSMOVIES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/arts/02LISTINGSMOVIES/02LISTINGSMOVIES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 251, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/02/arts/02LISTINGSMOVIES/02LISTINGSMOVIES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 251}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'cr