ca.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Publicly commemorating an album’s 10th anniversary is not the most brash rock ’n’ roll move, but forgive the Hold Steady and its fans for feeling nostalgic. This week the band roared back into Brooklyn (“roar” is perhaps the only gear it possesses) for four sold-out concerts, Wednesday through Saturday, at the Brooklyn Bowl, with a particular focus on its third — and breakout — album, “Boys and Girls in America,” from 2006.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/03/arts/03HOLDSTEADY1/03HOLDSTEADY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/03/arts/03HOLDSTEADY1/03HOLDSTEADY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/03/arts/03HOLDSTEADY1/03HOLDSTEADY1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/03/arts/03HOLDSTEADY1/03HOLDSTEADY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/03/arts/03HOLDSTEADY1/03HOLDSTEADY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/03/arts/03HOLDSTEADY1/03HOLDSTEADY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/03/arts/03HOLDSTEADY1/03HOLDSTEADY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1378, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Together Again, for Now: The Hold Steady in Brooklyn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Together Again, for Now: Hold Steady in Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hold Steady (Music Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finn, Craig (1971- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nicolay, Franz (1977- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Bowl', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-02T22:06:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e577be66-eac0-5a3b-aa30-19bcbd92c7bb', 'word_count': 805, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e577be66-eac0-5a3b-aa30-19bcbd92c7bb'}, {'abstract': 'How does a progressive company find itself pitched on a hard-right website? A third-party ad network is using consumer data and targeting technology.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/02/business/media/breitbart-vanguard-ads-follow-users-target-marketing.html', 'snippet': 'How does a progressive company find itself pitched on a hard-right website? A third-party ad network is using consumer data and targeting technology.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Vanguard Group does its best to stay away from politics when advertising, going so far as to have a policy against marketing on overtly partisan websites. So it was a surprise to Vanguard, an investme