ation': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ed84c13-3848-57ee-aa95-dcddaf6bbebf', 'word_count': 819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ed84c13-3848-57ee-aa95-dcddaf6bbebf'}, {'abstract': 'In one Belgian town, a mayor is committed to getting right what it seems like everyone else in Europe is getting wrong.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/03/opinion/sunday/where-refugees-can-come-home.html', 'snippet': 'In one Belgian town, a mayor is committed to getting right what it seems like everyone else in Europe is getting wrong.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MECHELEN, Belgium — The 20-foot-high effigy of a refugee perched on a rooftop here does not have a name. To his creators, the anonymity of the figure crouched in an orange life vest, his arms wrapped tightly around his knees, reflects the universality of his plight. But it also reflects the way many Europeans view the refugees and migrants arriving in their towns and cities: a nameless mass threatening their way of life.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/opinion/sunday/04mcdonaldgibson3-web/04mcdonaldgibson3-web-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/04/opinion/sunday/04mcdonaldgibson3-web/04mcdonaldgibson3-web-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/opinion/sunday/04mcdonaldgibson3-web/04mcdonaldgibson3-web-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/04/opinion/sunday/04mcdonaldgibson3-web/04mcdonaldgibson3-web-articleL