oks', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b38f6ea-de43-5bc1-8879-62b6ba76942a', 'word_count': 1038, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b38f6ea-de43-5bc1-8879-62b6ba76942a'}, {'abstract': 'Completing four rounds would have been seen as an unqualified success for Woods at the start of the Hero World Challenge, but he raised expectations significantly with his play.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/04/sports/tiger-woods-finishes-15th-hero-world-challenge.html', 'snippet': 'Completing four rounds would have been seen as an unqualified success for Woods at the start of the Hero World Challenge, but he raised expectations significantly with his play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NASSAU, the Bahamas — Tiger Woods raised his putter in celebration, so sure was he that his 40-foot birdie effort would be swallowed by the cup on the third hole of his final round of the Hero World Challenge. When the ball came up short, Woods dropped the club.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/05/sports/05CROUSEweb1/05CROUSEweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/05/sports/05CROUSEweb1/05CROUSEweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/05/sports/05CROUSEweb1/05CROUSEweb1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None,