lue': 'University of California', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berkeley (Calif)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sierra Nevada Region (US)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-04T22:45:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb6977b5-96f7-51c9-8ee8-52ec8746be4d', 'word_count': 907, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb6977b5-96f7-51c9-8ee8-52ec8746be4d'}, {'abstract': 'There were highlights as choreographers brought “One the Road,” “Meet Ella” and “[Insert Title]” to the stage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/04/arts/dance/rendering-on-the-road-as-dance-that-and-other-audacities.html', 'snippet': 'There were highlights as choreographers brought “One the Road,” “Meet Ella” and “[Insert Title]” to the stage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our downtown choreographers do not lack nerve. (In New York, “downtown” dance includes Brooklyn.) With fabulous hubris, the choreographer Zvi Gotheiner, in his new piece, “On the Road,” has tried rendering Jack Kerouac’s 1957 novel as dance theater. With equal daring, the dancer-choreographer Caleb Teicher has set his new tap dance, “Meet Ella,” to recordings of Ella Fitzgerald at her most incandescent, live in Rome (1958) and Berlin (1960).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/05/arts/05DANCENOTEBOOK-REFER/05DANCENOTEBOOK-REFER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thum