 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed8bc3d7-bf62-5341-b6bf-f8e9f7efab91', 'word_count': 741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed8bc3d7-bf62-5341-b6bf-f8e9f7efab91'}, {'abstract': 'The artist Gabe Leonard talks about a painting he created for a poster promoting the Los Angeles production of the play “Mom’s Dead.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/04/theater/moms-a-corpse-dad-looks-mad-at-least-the-light-is-nice.html', 'snippet': 'The artist Gabe Leonard talks about a painting he created for a poster promoting the Los Angeles production of the play “Mom’s Dead.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The painter Gabe Leonard loves big hands. Fists bigger than heads and fingers longer than legs factor prominently in his cinematic depictions of outlaws, mobsters and card sharks. So it makes sense that a giant fist — gripping a pitchfork and a cigarette — is front and center in an oil painting that became a poster for a production of Nathan Wellman’s play “Mom’s Dead.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/23/theater/poster-mom/poster-mom-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/23/theater/poster-mom/poster-mom-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/23/theater/poster-mom/poster-mom-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/23/theater/poster-mom/poster-mom-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 840, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/23/theater/poster-mom/poster-mom-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargew