ld the country’s banks and to help them deal with problem loans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/05/business/italy-referendum-euro-markets.html', 'snippet': 'The results of an Italian vote will probably postpone plans to rebuild the country’s banks and to help them deal with problem loans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Financial markets were stoic on Monday after Italian voters decisively rejected changes to their country’s Constitution intended to speed government decision-making and spur Italy’s stagnant economy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Markets Weather Italy Referendum Result, but Banks Are Vulnerable', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Renzi, Matteo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-05T07:49:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/224964e4-bddc-5804-9068-fd5c2754ba88', 'word_count': 989, 'uri': 'nyt://article/224964e4-bddc-5804-9068-fd5c2754ba88'}, {'abstract': 'The mysteries of the show start to clear up a little, with the twists in the finale intended to shock the hosts, not the viewers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/05/arts/television/westworld-season-finale-recap.html', 'snippet': 'The mysteries of the show start to clear up a little, with the twists in the finale intended to shock the hosts, not the viewers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Much like the center of the maze, we’ve been progressing toward a revelation in “Westworld” that’s been teasingly within our grasp all along. We’ve been making discoveries right alongside the hosts — discoveries about their origins and creators, about their capabilities, about their evolving sense of awareness about their true selves and the world around them. That last part has been immensely disturbing, given that some of our hosts have come to understand their function in the park as passive, defenseless objects of violence and sexual fantasy, doomed to live excruciating and frequently tragic loops. But the journey has been necessary to get them to a place where they can achieve full self-awareness and control their own destiny. Dolores gets there, and Westworld will never be the same.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/05/arts/television/05westworld/05westworld-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/05/arts/television/05westworld/05westworld-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/05/arts/television/05westworld/05westworld-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/05/arts/television/05westworld/05westworld-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy'