rganizations', 'value': 'Kennedy, John F, Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Renzi, Matteo', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-05T15:41:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vanessa Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vanessa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52065b6e-0caa-597e-861d-5b619130b6f2', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52065b6e-0caa-597e-861d-5b619130b6f2'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: Dom Pedro, the second Emperor of Brazil, dies of pneumonia while in exile, in December 1891.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/12/05/1891-dom-pedro-dead/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: Dom Pedro, the second Emperor of Brazil, dies of pneumonia while in exile, in December 1891.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dom Pedro, second Emperor of Brazil, has died in exile, while the country over which he reigned for fifty-eight years is still feeling the effects of a revolution which has cost more lives than did that by which this too easy-going ruler was expelled in 1889. It was at 12.30 this morning that the ex-Emperor passed away, the victim of a disease which, at first, was not considered dangerous, and which has lasted less than a week. Dom Pedro took a chill on leaving the Academy of Moral and Political Sciences eight days ago, and this developed into pneumonia. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/05/blogs/05oldiht-1891-dompedro/05oldiht-1891-dompedro-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/05/blogs/05oldiht-1891-dompedro/05oldiht-1891-dompedro-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/05/blogs/05oldiht-1891-dompedro/05oldiht-1891-dompedro-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/05/blogs/05oldiht-1891-dompedro/05oldiht-1891-dompedro-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 877, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/05/blogs/05oldiht-1891-dompedro/05oldiht-1891-dompedro-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 877}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/05/blogs/05oldiht-1891-dompedro/05oldiht-1891-dompedro-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 899, 'width': 615, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/05/blogs/05oldiht-1891-dompedro/05oldiht-1891-dompedro-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 899, 'width': 615, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1891: Dom Pedro Dead', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-05T15:42:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname'