z lured Etan into the basement of a bodega in 1979 and strangled him, and has been racked with guilt ever since.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The prosecution started its case with a mother recounting the last moments she spent with her young son, seeing him off one morning in 1979 on the short walk from his family’s loft in Manhattan to the school bus stop alone for the first time. The 6-year-old boy, Etan Patz, left with his toy cars in his tote bag, she recalled, and a dollar bill in his hand so he could buy a soda at the corner bodega.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/nyregion/02patz1/02patz1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/02/nyregion/02patz1/02patz1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/nyregion/02patz1/02patz1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/nyregion/02patz1/02patz1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/02/nyregion/02patz1/02patz1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/nyregion/02patz1/02patz1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/02/nyregion/02patz1/02patz1-superJumbo.jpg', 'h