rd_count': 892, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f640054-d987-5281-871f-1b543483270d'}, {'abstract': 'The unusual preserve is a family recipe from the founders of AnnaMaria’s Foods.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/05/dining/italian-jams-radicchio-marmalade-annamarias-foods.html', 'snippet': 'The unusual preserve is a family recipe from the founders of AnnaMaria’s Foods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This new line of jams in jewel-like colors is made from old Italian family recipes byDominique Debroux and her mother, Anne Marie Debroux, originally from Turin, Italy. An unusual radicchio marmalade is purple, with tart, cabbage flavors; the deep garnet strawberry-rose jam has an alluring fragrance; the tart-sweet almond-apricot jam exudes an irresistible perfume; and the thick, bright red bell pepper jam has a touch of heat. All can dress your morning toast, be served with roasted meats, accompany cheeses or make lovely gifts: Jams from AnnaMaria’s Foods, in eight-ounce jars, are $11 each at annamariasfoods.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/dining/07BURNER-JAM/07BURNER-JAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/07/dining/07BURNER-JAM/07BURNER-JAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/dining/07BURNER-JAM/07BURNER-JAM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/dining/07BURNER-JAM/07BURNER-JAM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 's