ne, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-12-05T17:46:06+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/a94c564a-72ca-5931-b4db-61cd581d6c51', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/a94c564a-72ca-5931-b4db-61cd581d6c51'}, {'abstract': 'The chef Pino Luongo returns to retail with a website dedicated to the tableware of Tuscany.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/05/dining/tuscan-platter-to-make-holiday-sweets-and-roasts-shine.html', 'snippet': 'The chef Pino Luongo returns to retail with a website dedicated to the tableware of Tuscany.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chef and restaurateur Pino Luongo’s new website, Simply Tuscan, echoes the gift shop of many years ago at Tuscan Square, his Rockefeller Center restaurant, which sold handsome tableware from the Italian region. His current restaurant, Morso, has no retail area, hence the website, which offers items for the kitchen and table imported from Italy. “It was successful at Tuscan Square, so I thought I’d try again,” he said. The site also features recipes and will eventually include specialty food products. For now, this lovely oblong platter, 8 by 15½ inches and perfect for that German stollen or French bûche de Noël, tops my list: Lastra rectangular platter, white or gray, $140, simply-tuscan.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/dining/07BURNER-PLATTER/07BURNER-PLATTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/07/dining/07BURNER-PLATTER/07BURNER-PLATTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'cap