tical physicist, was honored by having a department of physics at one of the nation’s leading public universities renamed after him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif of Pakistan honored Abdus Salam, a theoretical physicist and Nobel laureate who belonged to a persecuted minority, by renaming a department of physics at one of the nation’s leading public universities after him on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistan’s Premier Honors Nobel Laureate From Persecuted Minority', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salam, Abdus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nobel Prizes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Physics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharif, Nawaz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-05T18:22:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de0db4d9-48fd-5e79-9753-57aad12e17f1', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de0db4d9-48fd-5e79-9753-57aad12e17f1'}, {'abstract': 'We asked readers — without any context — to caption a photo that ran in The New York Times. Here’s how they responded.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/05/insider/times-insider-photo-challenge-caption-this.html', 'snippet': 'We asked readers — without any context — to caption a photo that ran in The New York Times. Here’s how they responded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Times Insider shares