[{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-05T18:29:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Insider', 'section_name': 'Times Insider', 'byline': {'original': 'By Insider Staff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Insider', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Staff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e0b5bb0-5215-58ae-9e0f-dd27a51bae22', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e0b5bb0-5215-58ae-9e0f-dd27a51bae22'}, {'abstract': 'The presence of many hundreds of veterans — organizers were anticipating 2,000 or more — adds another potent layer to a fight that is already steeped in sharp contrasts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/05/us/veterans-north-dakota-standing-rock.html', 'snippet': 'The presence of many hundreds of veterans — organizers were anticipating 2,000 or more — adds another potent layer to a fight that is already steeped in sharp contrasts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORT YATES, N.D. — After four deployments to Iraq and Afghanistan, after being hit by a roadside bomb and losing two friends to explosions, Jason Brocar floated from job to job, earning enough to pay for long solo hikes where his only worries were what he would eat and where he would sleep. He was deep into a rainy trek through Scotland when he noticed friends back home talking about a place called Standing Rock.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As North Dakota Pipeline Is Blocked, Veterans at Standing Rock Cheer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Veterans at Standing Rock Cheer Pipeline Decision', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Standing Rock Sioux Reservation (ND-SD)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pipelines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Native Americans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARMY CORPS OF ENGINEERS', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Transfer Partners LP', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Dakota', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-05T18:52:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ab0bbe3-07c5-54a8-9adf-536d9b0cb0eb', 'word_count': 1059, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ab0bbe3-07c5-54a8-9adf-536d9b0cb0eb'}, {'abstract': 'The artist Oliver Jeffers debuts a product line in Paris based on his 2014 book “Once Upon the Alphabet.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/05/t-magazine/art/oliver-jeffers-colette-clothes-toys.html', 'snippet': 'The artist Oliver Jeffers debuts a product line in Paris based on his 2014 book “Once Upon the Alphabet.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Oliver Jeffers’s 2014 book “Once Upon the Alphabet,” “A” isn’t for “apple” nor “aardvark,” but instead for an astronaut named Edmund, who had “been training to go on an adventure up into space to meet some aliens.” The assonant tale of Edmund’s acrophobia pans out in a few pages, before it’s on to “B: Burning a Bridge,” a brief history of the embattled neighbors Bernard and Bob. “My sketchbooks are filled with little ideas, and this is an amalgamation of 26 of them, each represented by one letter of the alphabet,” Jeffers says of the best seller. “The stories individually wouldn’t have worked as full picture books, but when combined create a whole.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/05/t-magazine/art/05tmag-oliver-jeffers-slide-788I/05tmag-oliver-jeffers-slide-788I-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/05/t-magazine/art/05tmag-oliver-jeffers-slide-788I/05tmag-oliver-jeffers-slide-788I-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/05/t-magazine/art/05tmag-oliver-jeffers-slide-788I/05tmag-oliver-jeffers-slide-788I-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/05/t-magazine/art/05tmag-oliver-jeffers-slide-788I/05tmag-oliver-jeffers-slide-788I-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 479, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/05/t-magazine/art/05tmag-oliver-jeffers-slide-788I/05tmag-oliver-jeffers-slide-788I-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 479}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/05/t-magazine/art/05tmag-oliver-jeffers-slide-788I/05tmag-oliver-jeffers-slide-788I-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 818, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2