: 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Wagner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wagner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4104aafd-f3d8-5d39-ac5b-de2d9721fd69', 'word_count': 806, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4104aafd-f3d8-5d39-ac5b-de2d9721fd69'}, {'abstract': 'Lt. Gen. Michael Flynn, Mr. Trump’s pick for national security adviser, has been in the habit of spreading pernicious conspiracy theories.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/05/opinion/fake-news-brings-a-gunman-to-washington.html', 'snippet': 'Lt. Gen. Michael Flynn, Mr. Trump’s pick for national security adviser, has been in the habit of spreading pernicious conspiracy theories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday afternoon, as families ate a late lunch at Comet Ping Pong in Washington, D.C., a man armed with a rifle walked in, aiming to “self-investigate” fake stories that the small pizzeria was a front for a child sex ring led by Hillary Clinton.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/opinion/06tue4web/06tue4web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/06/opinion/06tue4web/06tue4web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/opinion/06tue4web/06tue4web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/opinion/06tue4web/04tue4web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/06/opinion/06tue4web/04tue4web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/opinion/06tue4web/04tue4web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/opinion/06tue4web/04tue4web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fake News Brings a Gunman to Washington', 'kicker': 'Editorial Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rumors and Misinformation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flynn, Michael T', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comet Ping Pong (Washington, DC, Restaurant)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-05T21:41:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Williamson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williamson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c502879-b16d-5c4a-bcf7-f9e548564389', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c502879-b16d-5c4a-bcf7-f9e548564389'}, {'abstract': 'The Electoral College is supposed to determine if a candidate is qualified to be president. Mr. Trump has not met its standards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/05/opinion/why-i-will-not-cast-my-electoral-vote-for-donald-trump.html', 'snippet': 'The Electoral College is supposed to determine if a candidate is qualified to be president. Mr. Trump has not met its standards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DALLAS — I am a Republican presidential elector, one of the 538 people asked to choose officially the president of the United States. Since the election, people have asked me to change my vote based on policy disagreements with Donald J. Trump. In some cases, they cite the popular vote difference. I do not think presidents-elect should be disqualified for policy disagreements. I do not think they should be disqualified because they won the Electoral College instead of the popular vote. However, now I am asked to cast a vote on Dec. 19 for someone who shows daily he is not qualified for the office.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/opinion/06suprun/06suprun-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/06/opinion/06suprun/06suprun-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/opinion/06suprun/06suprun-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/opinion/06suprun/06suprun-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/06/opinion/06suprun/06suprun-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/opinion/06suprun/06suprun-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/opinion/06suprun/06suprun-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1797, 'width': 1797, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why I Will Not Cast My Electoral Vote for Donald Trump', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Electors Should Reject Trump', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suprun, Christopher', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electoral College', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-05T21:41:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Suprun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suprun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/122f698b-b7a4-5094-b8d7-7149dfe44ec9', 'word_count': 823, 'uri': 'nyt://article/122f698b-b7a4-5094-b8d7-7149dfe44ec9'}, {'abstract': 'A new handcrafted tequila, Siembra Valles Ancestral, is ready for the rocks glass.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/05/dining/tequila-siembra-valles-ancestral.html', 'snippet': 'A new handcrafted tequila, Siembra Valles Ancestral, is ready for the rocks glass.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This new tequila from David Suro’s Siembra Spirits provides a counterpoint to the many overrefined, vodkalike tequilas on the market. For his Siembra Valles Ancestral, blue agave hearts are roasted in hand-dug pits and mashed with wooden mallets, and the distillate is rested in large containers covered in corncobs, a traditional method that “allows the spirit to mellow properly,” Mr. Suro said. The result has a softly vegetal aroma, with hints of pineapple and smoke. It’s smooth and fruity, with a brash white-pepper kick. Savor it straight or on the rocks, with a squirt of lime or blood orange juice: Siembra Valles Ancestral, 50.2 percent alcohol, $124.96 at Astor Wine & Spirits, astorwines.com, siembraspirits.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/dining/07BURNER-TEQUILA/07BURNER-TEQUILA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/07/dining/07BURNER-TEQUILA/07BURNER-TEQUILA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/dining/07BURNER-TEQUILA/07BURNER-TEQUILA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/dining/07BURNER-TEQUILA/07BURNER-TEQUILA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1214, 'width': 60