 a police operation last year that involved sealing off the 22-mile Hangzhou Bay Bridge, one of the world’s longest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/06/business/international/china-xu-insider-trading-zexi.html', 'snippet': 'Xu Xiang was detained in a police operation last year that involved sealing off the 22-mile Hangzhou Bay Bridge, one of the world’s longest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHANGHAI — One of China’s best-known financiers, sometimes called his country’s equivalent to Carl C. Icahn, has pleaded guilty to insider trading and stock price manipulation, in a case that forms part of a broader nationwide push against financial improprieties.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top Chinese Financier Pleads Guilty to Insider Trading', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Star Investor in China Pleads Guilty to Misdeeds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradsher, Keith', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zexi Investment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xu Xiang', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-06T14:45:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a840fa0-1e08-528d-b747-fc7c46979fc9', 'word_count': 683, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a840fa0-1e08-528d-b747-fc7c46979fc9'}, {'abstract': 'The ruling brings to an end a bitter dispute between the government and energy firms over the decision in 2011 to abandon nuclear power in the wake of a nuclear disaster in Japan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/06/world/europe/germany-nuclear-power-court.html', 'snippet': 'The ruling brings to an end a bitter dispute between the government and energy firms over the decision in 2011 to abandon nuclear power in the wake of a nuclear disaster in Japan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — Germany’s highest court on Tuesday upheld the government’s decision in 2011 to shut its nuclear reactors ahead of schedule, but it ruled that power companies must be compensated for losses incurred as a result of that decision.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/world/07Germanynuclear/07Germanynuclear-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/07/world/07Germanynuclear/07Germanynuclear-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/world/07Germanynuclear/07Germanynuclear-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/world/07Germanynuclear/07Germanynuclear-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/07/world/07Germanynuclear/07Germanynuclear-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'ima