e', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/technology/07xp-INSTAGRAM/07xp-INSTAGRAM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/technology/07xp-INSTAGRAM/07xp-INSTAGRAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/06/technology/07xp-INSTAGRAM/07xp-INSTAGRAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/technology/07xp-INSTAGRAM/07xp-INSTAGRAM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/technology/07xp-INSTAGRAM/07xp-INSTAGRAM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1368, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Instagram Introduces New Tools Meant to Curb Abuse and Expand Privacy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberharassment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Instagram Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-06T15:29:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Rogers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rogers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eaa692f1-43cd-58bb-8455-cc756aa72d7e', 'word_count': 438, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eaa692f1-43cd-58bb-8455-cc756aa72d7e'}, {'abstract': 'Although Armenians are Christian and Azeris are Muslim, as I witnessed on my trip to Nagorno-Karabakh, the conflict has little to do with religion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/06/opinion/my-proud-pilgrimage-to-my-homeland.html', 'snippet': 'Although Armenians are Christian and Azeris are Muslim, as I witnessed on my trip to Nagorno-Karabakh, the conflict has little to do with religion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The forward trenches in the hills just beyond the abandoned village of Talish, in Nagorno-Karabakh, are reminiscent of World War I: long, endless, slits in the ground, the dirt buttressed by wood, with periodic firing posts and dugouts. Stacked tires packed with dirt stand in for sandbags, but otherwise it looks like the Western Front 100 years ago. Behind the trenches, alongside the road, tanks are angled to counterattack.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/07bohjalian2-inyt/07bohjalian2-inyt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/07bohjalian2-inyt/07bohjalian2-inyt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/07bohjalian2-inyt/07bohjalian2-inyt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/07bohjalian2-inyt/07bohjalian2-inyt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/07bohjalian2-inyt/07bohjalian2-inyt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/07bohjalian2-inyt/07bohjalian2-inyt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/07bohjalian2-inyt/07bohjalian2-inyt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Proud Pilgrimage to My Homeland', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A proud pilgrimage to my homeland', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nagorno-Karabakh', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Armenians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-06T15:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Bohjalian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bohjalian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7dd8b0a6-e4f3-564d-9274-70f444a1cb0b', 'word_count': 1211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7dd8b0a6-e4f3-564d-9274-70f444a1cb0b'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: Mr. Lloyd George resigns his Secretary of State position and British Prime Minister Asquith resigns shortly after, in December 1916.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/12/06/1916-mr-lloyd-george-resigns/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: Mr. Lloyd George resigns his Secretary of State position and British Prime Minister Asquith resigns shortly after, in December 1916.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The Government crisis developed to-day with dramatic swiftness. First of all came the news that Mr. Lloyd George had resigned his position as Secretary of State for War owing to the fact that the Premier had firmly declined to accept his proposal for the formation of a War Council from which he, Mr. Asquith, would be excluded. This announcement was followed shortly afterwards by an official inti\xadmation that Mr. Asquith had tendered his resignation to the King, and later it was announced that His Majesty had accepted. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/blogs/06oldiht-1916-lloyd/06oldiht-1916-lloyd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 288, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/06/blogs/06oldiht-1916-lloyd/06oldiht-1916-lloyd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 288}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/blogs/06oldiht-1916-lloyd/06oldiht-1916-lloyd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 324, 'width': 676, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/blogs/06oldiht-1916-lloyd/06oldiht-1916-lloyd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 324, 'width': 676, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/blogs/06oldiht-1916-lloyd/06oldiht-1916-lloyd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/06/blogs/06oldiht-1916-lloyd/06oldiht-1916-lloyd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/blogs/06oldiht-1916-lloyd/06oldiht-1916-lloyd-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1916: Mr. Lloyd George Resigns', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-06T15:42:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0dad430-7c9b-5cd7-9f7c-ad878bdae045', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0dad430-7c9b-5cd7-9f7c-ad878bdae045'}, {'abstract': 'One of the bloc’s chief negotiators said that there would be no “cherry picking” by Britain and that a deal needed to be reached within 18 months of talks opening.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/06/world/europe/brexit-uk-eu.html', 'snippet': 'One of the bloc’s chief negotiators said that there would be no “cherry picking” by Britain and that a deal needed to be reached within 18 months of talks opening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — For months, Britain’s government has suggested that, when the country leaves the European Union, it will be able to retain many of the economic advantages of membership in the bloc.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/world/07Brexit1/07Brexit1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/07/world/07Brexit1/07Brexit1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/world/07Brexit1/07Brexit1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/world/07Brexit1/07Brexit1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/07/world/07Brexit1/07Brexit1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/world/07Brexit1/07Brexit1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/world/07Brexit1/07Brexit1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1369, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'E.U. Leaders Talk Tough on ‘Brexit’ and Warn That Time Is Short', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'E.U. Leaders  Talk Tough  on ‘Brexit’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castle, Stephen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Great Britain Withdrawal from EU (Brexit)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kanter, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barnier, Michel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'May, Theresa M', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-06T15:51:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Kanter and Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kanter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9c5296b-554e-5dab-813a-e36fd01b72d6', 'word_count': 707, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9c5296b-554e-5dab-813a-e36fd01b72d6'}, {'abstract': 'In a message that seemed to come out of the blue, Mr. Trump took to Twitter to object to Boeing’s plans for a next-generation presidential plane.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/06/us/politics/trump-air-force-one-boeing.html', 'snippet': 'In a message that seemed to come out of the blue, Mr. Trump took to Twitter to object to Boeing’s plans for a next-generation presidential plane.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President-elect Donald J. Trump took a shot on Tuesday at one of the nation’s largest manufacturers, Boeing, sharply criticizing a pending order for a new Air Force One and suggesting that the company was “doing a little bit of a number” with the cost of the next generation of presidential aircraft.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Cancel Order!’ Donald Trump Attacks Plans for Upgraded Air Force One', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trump Attacks Plan to Update Air Force One', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIR FORCE ONE (JET)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drew, Christopher', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boeing Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Air Force', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-06T15:58:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear and Christopher Drew', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f743d9a0-583c-571b-b429-b4fdffbebe47', 'word_count': 1320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f743d9a0-583c-571b-b429-b4fdffbebe47'}, {'abstract': 'Polina Davydova was 3 when her family escaped the Nazis, and 53 when she left Russia. Now 77 and in failing health, she is grateful for the generosity of her new country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/06/nyregion/neediest-cases-fund-russia.html', 'snippet': 'Polina Davydova was 3 when her family escaped the Nazis, and 53 when she left Russia. Now 77 and in failing health, she is grateful for the generosity of her new country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Under the cover of night, the family crowded