12/06/dining/best-cookbooks-baking.html', 'snippet': 'Six dessert books push the genre into new territory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the world of baking cookbooks, the ones written by pastry chefs are glamorous things, filled with the caramel-spangled drama you would expect to see at the end of a 12-course tasting menu. But however ambitious they are on the page, the recipes often fall short in the kitchen, leaving a frustrated cook amid a trail of fallen soufflés.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Year’s Best Baking Cookbooks: Radical Ideas, Classic Treats', 'kicker': 'Cookbooks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Let the Bakers Bake', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Melissa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cookies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-06T21:13:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b96fb1dd-2065-517b-9d39-5c6682c02d07', 'word_count': 1237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b96fb1dd-2065-517b-9d39-5c6682c02d07'}, {'abstract': 'Stephen Starr and chef Daniel Rose, whose New York restaurant Le Coucou received critical acclaim this year, quietly reopened a small Parisian spot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/06/t-magazine/food/chez-la-vieille-paris-stephen-starr.html', 'snippet': 'Stephen Starr and chef Daniel Rose, whose New York restaurant Le Coucou received critical acclaim this year, quietly reopened a small Parisian spot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you’re behind one of the most praised new restaurants in New York City, perhaps even in the country, what comes next? For Stephen Starr, the megawatt restaurant mogul from Philadelphia, and chef Daniel Rose, a Parisian by way of Chicago, who together opened the highly acclaimed French restaurant Le Coucou over the summer, the answer is to simply open another restaurant. But this time in Paris, in an old bistro that was originally opened in 1958.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/t-magazine/food/06tmag-stephen-starr-slide-GP9X/06tmag-stephen-starr-slide-GP9X-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/06/t-magazine/food/06tmag-stephen-starr-slide-GP9X/06tmag-stephen-starr-slide-GP9X-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/t-magazine/food/06tmag-stephen-starr-slide-GP9X/06tmag-stephen-starr-slide-GP9X-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/06/t-magazine/food/06tmag-stephen-starr-slide-GP9X/06tmag-stephen-starr-slide-GP9X-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/06/t-magazine/food/06tmag-stephen-starr-slide-GP9X/06tmag-stephen-starr-slide-GP9X-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'c