 in SoHo, and other restaurant news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/06/dining/dan-kluger-loring-place-restaurant-openings.html', 'snippet': 'Salvation Burger reopens, a longtime Parisian establishment pops up in SoHo, and other restaurant news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LORING PLACE At 43, the chef Dan Kluger, who has worked in the kitchens of many top names, was eager to be on his own and get his new restaurant off the ground. But compromises were not on his agenda, so it wound up taking two years. Even finding a name was, as he put it, “a struggle.” (It’s the street in the Fordham section of the Bronx where his father lived.) The spacious double storefront from 1848, on the increasingly attractive stretch of Eighth Street west of Fifth Avenue, looks as if it was worth the wait. Whitewashed brick walls contain a barroom and a bilevel dining room decorated simply, with a nod to midcentury modern. Mr. Kluger’s food is seasonal and market driven. And it builds on his experience working with chefs like Floyd Cardoz at Tabla, which shapes the flavors in his suckling pig and on his cauliflower with Indian seasonings, and Jean-Georges Vongerichten at ABC Kitchen, which inspired a vegetable focus on the menu. Local sourcing is so important to him that he’s grinding wheat from upstate for pasta extruded in-house. (Opens Saturday): 21 West Eighth Street, 212-388-1831, loringplacenyc.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/dining/07OFF/07OFF-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/07/dining/07OFF/07OFF-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/dining/07OFF/07OF