: 'By Dana Thomas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d295ebd4-946f-5f8c-8334-2a14e51a5aa7', 'word_count': 1167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d295ebd4-946f-5f8c-8334-2a14e51a5aa7'}, {'abstract': 'The chairman of the luxury group Richemont said the disappearance of traditional skills had prompted him to act.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/07/fashion/craftsmanship-johann-rupert-richemont.html', 'snippet': 'The chairman of the luxury group Richemont said the disappearance of traditional skills had prompted him to act.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — “Our society today honors all the wrong people. Those who do good now live on the last pages of the newspaper. Then there are these footballers making millions. Fashion designers who just stand on the end of a catwalk after a show. Or women who sit on a front row and are paid to wear ridiculous clothes. It really makes us shudder, the level some people will go to for attention. I’m sorry, it is so banal. Where are our values?”', 'print_section': 'S', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/style/07michaelangelo01-inyt/07michaelangelo01-inyt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/07/style/07michaelangelo01-inyt/07michaelangelo01-inyt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/style/07michaelangelo01-inyt/07michaelangelo01-inyt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 's