when a parent is not responding to a child’s distress, what to do when a friend befriends your rapist’s ex and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/07/magazine/do-you-get-involved-when-a-parent-treats-a-child-badly.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on whether to intervene when a parent is not responding to a child’s distress, what to do when a friend befriends your rapist’s ex and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was walking home from dinner with a friend one evening down a quiet residential street. Two boys, ages somewhere between 8 and 10, were biking down the road accompanied by a middle-aged woman. I assumed she was their mother. The front wheel of the second boy’s bike took a glancing blow from the curb and sent its rider straight onto the sidewalk. The boy, nursing what looked like a bruised knee and ego, held back tears.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/magazine/11ethicist/11mag-11ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/11/magazine/11ethicist/11mag-11ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/magazine/11ethicist/11mag-11ethicist-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/magazine/11ethicist/11mag-11ethicist-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 454, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/magazine/11ethicist/11mag-11ethicist-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 454, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Do You Get Involved When a Parent Treats a Child Badly?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Do I Get Involved When a Parent Treats a Child Badly?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appiah, Kwame Anthony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicist, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-07T10:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a066903-5227-57d4-8247-c082c7e77e87', 'word_count': 1455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a066903-5227-57d4-8247-c082c7e77e87'}, {'abstract': 'The pleasures of your own personal horror movie, on repeat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/07/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-anxiety-dreams.html', 'snippet': 'The pleasures of your own personal horror movie, on repeat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is incredible to me how little I remember of what I was taught in high school. Whole subjects, entire years, have just dissolved. I need a calculator to do any kind of multiplication now. I recently tried to explain how electricity worked to a small child, and even she could tell I was making it up. But there are two things I recall with exceptional clarity: Napoleon’s retreat from Moscow (the hunger, the cold, the sleeping bags made of horse carcasses), and the opening soliloquy of “Richard III,” which I was required to memorize for English class at 16. I took this request very seriously, because I was not cool, and I spent many days slinking up and down the corridors hissing, “I am determined to prove a villain” to myself and narrowing my eyes. Though my ability to recite it remains useful as a party trick, that is not the reason it has remained lodged in my mind.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/magazine/11lor/11lor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/11/magazine/11lor/11lor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/magazine/11lor/11lor-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/magazine/11lor/11mag-11lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/11/magazine/11lor/11mag-11lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 436}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/magazine/11lor/11mag-11lor-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 744, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/magazine/11lor/11mag-11lor-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1488, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter of Recommendation: Anxiety Dreams', 'kicker': 'Letter of Recommendation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Anxiety Dreams ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lyster, Rosa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dreams', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richard III, King of England', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-07T10:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rosa Lyster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rosa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86de2b36-ace6-5bc7-85bf-c9ce48df6b20', 'word_count': 975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86de2b36-ace6-5bc7-85bf-c9ce48df6b20'}, {'abstract': 'As the oldest of us millennials begin to flee screaming from our 20s, where’s our “voice of a generation” novel?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/07/books/review/why-theres-no-millennial-novel.html', 'snippet': 'As the oldest of us millennials begin to flee screaming from our 20s, where’s our “voice of a generation” novel?', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the oldest of us millennials begin to flee screaming from our 20s, it seems we may have forgotten something — where’s our “voice of a generation” novel? One of those all-important lifestyle accessories that supposedly speak to, and for, the sensibilities and circumstances of an entire American cohort? Not only is the current front-runner, Lena Dunham, not even a novelist, but her fictional avatar in “Girls” dismisses the idea of such a generational voice in the show’s very first episode.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '37', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/books/review/1211-BKS-CriticsTake/1211-BKS-CriticsTake-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/11/books/review/1211-BKS-CriticsTake/1211-BKS-CriticsTake-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/books/review/1211-BKS-CriticsTake/1211-BKS-CriticsTake-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/books/review/1211-BKS-CriticsTake/1211-BKS-CriticsTake-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 610, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/11/books/review/1211-BKS-CriticsTake/1211-BKS-CriticsTake-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 610}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/books/review/1211-BKS-CriticsTake/1211-BKS-CriticsTake-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1007, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/books/review/1211-BKS-CriticsTake/1211-BKS-CriticsTake-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2014, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why There’s No ‘Millennial’ Novel', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Take', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Missing Millennial Novel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Millennial Generation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Age, Chronological', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-07T10:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tony Tulathimutte', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tulathimutte', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d60ae4a-5105-580f-ada6-14cdf8a2d94e', 'word_count': 766, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d60ae4a-5105-580f-ada6-14cdf8a2d94e'}, {'abstract': 'What to do if your father is the Super Mario Brothers bandit, or a narcissistic biologist who collects scorpions? Or if your blind black parents join a white-supremacist church?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/07/books/review/all-in-the-family.html', 'snippet': 'What to do if your father is the Super Mario Brothers bandit, or a narcissistic biologist who collects scorpions? Or if your blind black parents join a white-supremacist church?', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s nothing like the holidays to make you grateful for family ties while also wishing you were related to no one. Fortunately, you needn’t look further than the memoir section of your local bookstore to be reminded that, as dysfunctional as your tribe is, someone out there not only has it worse bu