d_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21963ce6-864f-5753-b425-c47b38d1545c'}, {'abstract': 'People here are ecstatic about the phone call between the U.S. president-elect and Taiwan’s president. But is the U.S. really ready for change?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/07/opinion/donald-trump-taiwan-phone-call-china.html', 'snippet': 'People here are ecstatic about the phone call between the U.S. president-elect and Taiwan’s president. But is the U.S. really ready for change?', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAIPEI, Taiwan — The atmosphere here is almost jubilant. The phone call last weekend from President Tsai Ing-wen of Taiwan to President-elect Donald J. Trump — the first contact between a Taiwanese president and an American president or president-elect since at least 1979 — has received rare bipartisan support here on this self-governing island off southern China. It was, many agree, a great thing for the country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/opinion/07allenSub/07allenSub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/07/opinion/07allenSub/07allenSub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/opinion/07allenSub/07allenSub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/opinion/07allenSub/07allenSub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/07/opinion/07allenSub/07allenSub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 