world of ballet for more than 40 years. After the company’s debut in 1974, critics applauded its smart satire of ballerinas and inherent commentary on the performance of femininity. But hidden in all that jest is great reverence for the art form and its history, and audiences keep coming back — when else can you laugh at the ballet?', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/arts/11GUIDE4/11GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/11/arts/11GUIDE4/11GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/arts/11GUIDE4/11GUIDE4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/arts/11GUIDE4/11GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/11/arts/11GUIDE4/11GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/arts/11GUIDE4/11GUIDE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/arts/11GUIDE4/11GUIDE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brawny Chests and Classic Tutus', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dance; Hairy Chests and Classic Tutus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Les Ballets Trockadero de Monte Carlo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joyce Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-07T17:22:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Schaefer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schaefer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41d037ad-110a-5a3c-b7f4-57d7a63a7f15', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41d037ad-110a-5a3c-b7f4-57d7a63a7f15'}, {'abstract': 'Rez Abbasi’s all-star project, Invocation, includes the pianist Vijay Iyer and will be playing the Asia Society.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/07/arts/music/a-guitarists-cultural-fusion-with-a-touch-of-play.html', 'snippet': 'Rez Abbasi’s all-star project, Invocation, includes the pianist Vijay Iyer and will be playing the Asia Society.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The guitarist Rez Abbasi, who was born in Pakistan but raised in Southern California, approaches the process of cultural fusion with deep seriousness but also a spirit of play. In his own groups — and with cooperatives like the Indo-Pak Coalition, an excellent trio featuring Rudresh Mahanthappa on alto saxophone and Dan Weiss on drums and percussion — he adds his dynamic, brisk voice to the modern-jazz dialect. Mr. Abbasi’s band Invocation, which features Mr. Mahanthappa and Mr. Weiss along with the pianist Vijay Iyer, the bassist Johannes Weidenmüller and the cellist Elizabeth Means, taps into the complex classical traditions of South Indian Carnatic music. On Thursday, Dec. 15, and Friday at Asia Society, they’ll play music from “Unfiltered Universe,” which Mr. Abbasi will release next year, completing a trilogy of albums by the band. (212-517-2742; asiasociety.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/arts/11GUIDE7/11GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/11/arts/11GUIDE7/11GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/arts/11GUIDE7/11GUIDE7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/arts/11GUIDE7/11GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/11/arts/11GUIDE7/11GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/arts/11GUIDE7/11GUIDE7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/arts/11GUIDE7/11GUIDE7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1420, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Guitarist’s Cultural Fusion, With a Touch of Play', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pop; Cultural Fusion All-Stars Ready', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'n