persons', 'value': 'Phillips, Randy (1954- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-07T18:44:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/adb80ed8-953d-59cb-9f6a-4afb26d57d41', 'word_count': 438, 'uri': 'nyt://article/adb80ed8-953d-59cb-9f6a-4afb26d57d41'}, {'abstract': 'This list includes feats of acting and core strength, performances that made the author happy even when they raised his blood pressure or made him cry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/07/arts/best-performances.html', 'snippet': 'This list includes feats of acting and core strength, performances that made the author happy even when they raised his blood pressure or made him cry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My 11-part collection of favorite performances might cover a lot of ground (movies, television, sports, the web) and include feats of both acting and core strength, but they all made me happy even when they raised my blood pressure or made me cry. Not included: Krisha Fairchild, the star of Trey Edward Shults’s movie “Krisha,” and Beyoncé at the Super Bowl, because I’ve said my piece (many times over!) about how outrageously good they are. I left the casts of “Moonlight” and “Atlanta” alone for pretty much the same reason. And I’m also sad for missing Jake Gyllenhaal in “Sunday in the Park With George,” Nina Stemme in “Tristan und Isolde” and Kathleen Battle make up with the Met. Word on the street is I should feel sorry for myself, and I do. Here’s what I did see, though:', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank'