, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-12-07T19:05:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NYTNow', 'section_name': 'Briefing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles McDermid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDermid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/3eeb3cb3-0f3d-5bc8-9e37-1d079aad48c5', 'word_count': 1067, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3eeb3cb3-0f3d-5bc8-9e37-1d079aad48c5'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Pruitt, the Oklahoma attorney general, has been a key architect of the legal battle against President Obama’s climate change policies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/07/us/politics/scott-pruitt-epa-trump.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Pruitt, the Oklahoma attorney general, has been a key architect of the legal battle against President Obama’s climate change policies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President-elect Donald J. Trump has selected Scott Pruitt, the Oklahoma attorney general and a close ally of the fossil fuel industry, to run the Environmental Protection Agency, signaling Mr. Trump’s determination to dismantle President Obama’s efforts to counter climate change — and much of the E.P.A. itself.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/08/us/08pruitt1/08pruitt1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/08/us/08pruitt1/08pruitt1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/08/us/08pruitt1/08pruitt1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thu