0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/6c185bba-c41b-5a86-b38c-135d8f31a878'}, {'abstract': 'Karl Lagerfeld presented a collection yesterday in the grand old hotel where Coco Chanel had lived for decades.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/07/t-magazine/fashion/chanel-metiers-d-art-ritz-hotel-karl-lagerfeld.html', 'snippet': 'Karl Lagerfeld presented a collection yesterday in the grand old hotel where Coco Chanel had lived for decades.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gabrielle “Coco” Chanel spent her life at the Paris Ritz — a fact much-publicized, mythologized and commercialized over her lifetime, and beyond. She died there on Jan. 10, 1971. And, in a manner, she was reborn there, too — as the great Parisian couturière, rather than the orphan girl from Saumur. Chanel was at the very height of her fame and influence when she took up residence at the Ritz permanently in 1937. She had already taken over the stretch of buildings Chanel still occupies, down the Rue Cambon, which runs along the back of the hotel itself, and at that point employed 4,000 people. Her multiple suites at the Ritz served as a symbol of her success.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/t-magazine/fashion/07tmag-chanel-slide-92J4/07tmag-chanel-slide-92J4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/07/t-magazine/fashion/07tmag-chanel-slide-92J4/07tmag-chanel-slide-92J4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/t-magazine/fashion/07tmag-chanel-slide-92J4/07tmag-chanel-slide-92J4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't