uperJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ryan McGinness’s ‘50 Parties’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-12-07T21:52:15+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/eb6eeb0c-c5f0-522f-9c57-212ee398fd22', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/eb6eeb0c-c5f0-522f-9c57-212ee398fd22'}, {'abstract': 'In 2009 and 2010, Ryan McGinness hosted 50 themed events at his studio, and photographed them for a new book. The project got a little out of control.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/07/t-magazine/art/ryan-mcginness-50-parties-art-basel-miami.html', 'snippet': 'In 2009 and 2010, Ryan McGinness hosted 50 themed events at his studio, and photographed them for a new book. The project got a little out of control.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Between 2009 and 2010, the artist Ryan McGinness embarked on an endurance performance in which he hosted one party a week in his New York studio for 50 consecutive weeks. (Fifty-one, if you count the practice party that kicked things off.) This turned out to be a more brutal exercise than initially intended. Last week, during Art Basel Miami Beach, McGinness sat at a table at the Standard Hotel and reflected on this experience. It was “harrowing and stressful,” he said. “Yeah, it was awful. After the second party I was ready to throw in the towel.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/t-magazine/art/07tmag-ryanmcginness-slide-V4Z5/07tmag-ryanmcginness-slide-V4Z5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/07/t-m