', 'snippet': 'The European Central Bank also said it would cut the size of the program next year, while insisting it had no plans to end asset purchases altogether.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT — The European Central Bank said on Thursday that it would buy large quantities of bonds and other assets for longer than planned but would cut the size of the purchases, a decision it insisted did not a signal that a much anticipated “tapering” of stimulus measures had begun.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'E.C.B. Extends Bond-Buying Program to Protect Eurozone Economy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'E.C.B. Extends Bond-Buying Program, but Says It Will Cut Size of Purchases', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Draghi, Mario', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-08T04:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1abbcc1b-7408-55de-9ae7-b25c51b761d4', 'word_count': 961, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1abbcc1b-7408-55de-9ae7-b25c51b761d4'}, {'abstract': 'Hannah and President Kirkman work to expose or cover up potentially damaging information.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/07/arts/television/designated-survivor-season-1-episode-9-recap.html', 'snippet': 'Hannah and President Kirkman work to expose or cover up potentially damaging information.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Designated Survivor” is moving at two simultaneous but very different rhythms. The F.B.I. agent Hannah Wells has raced through reveal after shocking reveal while President Kirkman has stumbled after her, wading through bureaucracy and banging his head fruitlessly on the nation’s largest mysteries. The show’s double-barreled plotline seemed to promise a powerful pact between the two — if Kirkman could just get his act together. But right as he uncovers a huge piece of evidence to accelerate that connection, the show takes a sharp left turn.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/watching/07designatedsurvivor/07designatedsurvivor-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/07/watching/07designatedsurvivor/07designatedsurvivor-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/watching/07designatedsurvivor/07designatedsurvivor-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/07/watching/07designatedsurvivor/07designatedsurvivor-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/07/watching/07designatedsurvivor/07designatedsurvivor-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': N