-overthrow-hussein/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: The Syrian president, Noureddin Atassi, offers arms to Jordanian rebels protesting against King Hussein in Damascus, in December 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT — Syria today offered arms to Jordanian “revolutionaries” to overthrow King Hussein. Syrian President Noureddin Atassi told thousands of anti-Hussein demonstrators in the streets of Damascus that “our weapons are available to those who want them.” “Today is the liberation of Jordan,” he said. “Tomorrow the liberation of Palestine.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1966: Syria Offers Aid to Rebels to Overthrow Hussein', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestine Liberation Organization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Damascus (Syria)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jordan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-08T15:42:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1961b5b7-3894-5379-9477-57da1df91894', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1961b5b7-3894-5379-9477-57da1df91894'}, {'abstract': 'Breaking down the barriers between high fashion and lowly activewear.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/08/fashion/mens-style/fashionable-gym-workout-clothes-for-men.html', 'snippet': 'Breaking down the barriers between high fashion and lowly activewear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a growing conflation of what you may wear for a workout and the ready-to-wear clothes on the runways of Milan and Paris. The designer Gosha Rubchinskiy, who has collaborated with the Italian sportswear company Kappa, and Vetements, which has worked with Reebok, have been leading the charge. And with sports-centric brands like Tracksmith, Soar and Outdoor Voices also offering chic versions of activewear, who’s to say what’s appropriate for the gym and what’s better left to more fashionable occasions?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Workout Gear Is Fashionable Enough for the Runway', 'kicker': 'Dress Codes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gym Class Heroes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vetements (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reebok International Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubchinskiy, Gosha', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-08T15:42:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Men’s Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Tudela', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tudela', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/267cb27f-bbbd-5e07-9f88-153a8c738ca4', 'word_count': 81, 'uri': 'nyt://article/267cb27f-bbbd-5e07-9f88-153a8c738ca4'}, {'abstract': 'Research shows that only half of Americans in their 30s earn more than their parents did at the same age. A few decades ago, nearly all adults did.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/08/opinion/the-american-dream-quantified-at-last.html', 'snippet': 'Research shows that only half of Americans in their 30s earn more than their parents did at the same age. A few decades ago, nearly all adults did.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The phrase “American dream” was invented during the Great Depression. It comes from a popular 1931 book by the historian James Truslow Adams, who defined it as “that dream of a land in which life should be better and richer and fuller for everyone.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/11leonhardt-web/11leonhardt-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/11leonhardt-web/11leonhardt-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/11leonhardt-web/11leonhardt-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/11leonhardt-web/11leonhardt-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 708, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/11leonhardt-web/11leonhardt-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 708}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/11leonhardt-web/11leonhardt-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 868, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'