5+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/6b8e2438-1dc1-548f-be8e-dd7d9658dd92', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/6b8e2438-1dc1-548f-be8e-dd7d9658dd92'}, {'abstract': 'The photographer Harley Weir — who shot her first fashion editorial for a magazine at age 17 — opened her first solo show in Amsterdam this month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/08/t-magazine/art/harley-weir-boundaries-photography-solo-show.html', 'snippet': 'The photographer Harley Weir — who shot her first fashion editorial for a magazine at age 17 — opened her first solo show in Amsterdam this month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether shooting a portfolio of Senegalese people at work and play or young women in varying states of undress, the images taken by the British photographer Harley Weir, 28, capture unguarded moments with an honest eye. In “Boundaries,” her first solo show — which opened at Amsterdam’s FOAM Museum earlier this month — Weir’s photos draw the viewer into proximity with her subjects, so that skin and emotion are magnified. “There’s definitely a sense of intimacy to my work,” she says. “That’s the strongest element.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/08/t-magazine/art/08tmag-harlyweir-slide-UF1E/08tmag-harlyweir-slide-UF1E-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/08/t-magazine/art/08tmag-harlyweir-slide-UF1E/08tmag-harlyweir-slide-UF1E-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/08/t-magazine/art/08tmag-harlyweir-s