rted', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/225ef39b-dfb1-5a9c-ad0c-a43eaafc00ef', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/225ef39b-dfb1-5a9c-ad0c-a43eaafc00ef'}, {'abstract': 'Frankie and Johnny’s story returns, written and directed by Matthew Ross, but not much has changed except the actors and how well they fit together.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/08/movies/frank-and-lola-review-michael-shannon-imogen-poots.html', 'snippet': 'Frankie and Johnny’s story returns, written and directed by Matthew Ross, but not much has changed except the actors and how well they fit together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Its title is an early tip-off that “Frank & Lola” will be a new riff on Frankie and Johnny’s old troubles. Immortalized in song and onstage, these two have lent their names and heartache to a couple of films. (The movie shares its title with a Jimmy Buffett song.) They’re back in shadow form in “Frank & Lola,” this time with an unpersuasively paired Michael Shannon and Imogen Poots as Las Vegas souls who, after tumbling into bed, fall for each other. Soon, Frank and Lola learn that love still hurts, especially when tendrils of jealously start twisting through the story and he confuses abandon with possession.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/09/arts/09FRANKLOLA/09FRANKLOLA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/09/arts/09FRANKLOLA/09FRANKLOLA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/09/arts/09FRANKLOLA/09FRANKLOLA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/09/arts/09FRANKLOLA/09FRANKLOLA-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 312, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/09/arts/09FRANKLOLA/09FRANKLOLA-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 312}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/09/arts/09FRANKLOLA/09FRANKLOLA-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/09/arts/09FRANKLOLA/09FRANKLOLA-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1066, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Frank & Lola,’ Retreading Old Ground', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tainted Love in Familiar Packaging', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shannon, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Frank & Lola (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ross, Matthew (1976- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poots, Imogen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-08T22:05:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/409a473e-d68c-58ba-9237-d4651a3dc6eb', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/409a473e