ub_date': '2016-12-08T23:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By DENNY LEE', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Denny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'LEE', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/85e8d7b9-3521-5877-a2c0-fc784357f320', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/85e8d7b9-3521-5877-a2c0-fc784357f320'}, {'abstract': 'Galas were held for the Committee to Protect Journalists, Berggruen Institute, Cold Spring Harbor Laboratory, and Food Allergy Research and Education.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/08/fashion/galas-committee-to-protect-journalists-berggruen-institute-cold-spring-harbor-laboratory-food-allergy-research-education.html', 'snippet': 'Galas were held for the Committee to Protect Journalists, Berggruen Institute, Cold Spring Harbor Laboratory, and Food Allergy Research and Education.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 19th annual Food Allergy Ball, which benefits Food Allergy Research and Education, was Dec. 5 at the Waldorf Astoria. The Berggruen Institute, a philosophical think tank based in Los Angeles, awarded the inaugural Berggruen Prize on Dec. 1 to the Canadian philosopher Charles Taylor at the New York Public Library; the $1 million award recognizes a living thinker of great influence. The Cold Spring Harbor Laboratory honored Alan Alda and P. Roy Vaglos at its Double Helix Medals ceremony Dec. 1 at the American Museum of Natural History. And the Committee to Protect Journalists held its International Press Freedom Awards on Nov. 22 at the Waldorf Astoria.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thinkers and Scientists', 'kicker': 'Party Coverage: Scene City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Thinkers and Scientists', 'name': None, '