l', 'snippet': 'The tiny, striking bird is an amiable partner on a walk, its familiar call welcome in the winter woods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent walk along the edge of a young Bronx woodland, I looked up to find that I was not alone. About six black-capped chickadees had turned a bare gray birch into a sort of Christmas tree. As additional birds flitted in, they chattered and jockeyed for position. Clearly investigating my activities, within a few seconds a dozen birds were no more than a yard or two away. It struck me that I’ve received holiday cards that looked a lot like this.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/nyregion/11NATURE1/11NATURE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/11/nyregion/11NATURE1/11NATURE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/nyregion/11NATURE1/11NATURE1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/nyregion/11NATURE1/11NATURE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/11/nyregion/11NATURE1/11NATURE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/nyregion/11NATURE1/11NATURE1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'cr