formation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-10T19:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e314848-3ce5-57a7-b82a-471c20b6600e', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e314848-3ce5-57a7-b82a-471c20b6600e'}, {'abstract': 'To effectively challenge the president-elect, writers and artists must present a compelling vision of the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/10/opinion/sunday/trump-is-a-great-storyteller-we-need-to-be-better.html', 'snippet': 'To effectively challenge the president-elect, writers and artists must present a compelling vision of the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My son is 3 years old. Every morning and evening I read to him. I love the joy he takes in learning new words, immersing himself in stories, seeing himself as the characters, and acquiring a moral and ethical sense. He lives in a fictional world of good and bad, of threat and rescue, of the choice between doing good or doing harm.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/11nguyen-web/11nguyen-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/11nguyen-web/11nguyen-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/11nguyen-web/11nguyen-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'cro