ere leaving the funeral of a relative when they got into a traffic altercation with an off-duty fireman. An off-duty police officer and a uniformed sergeant joined the fray. When Mr. Beal “failed to drop his weapon,” he was shot multiple times by one or both of the officers.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/11austen/11austen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/11austen/11austen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/11austen/11austen-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/11austen/11austen-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/11austen/11austen-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/11austen/11austen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/11/opinion/sunday/11austen/11austen-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1380, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Violence and Division on Chicago’s South Side', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Violence and Division on Chicago’s South Side', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ben', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (Chicago, Ill)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-10T19:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7038e431-a5d5-5c7b-9467-26f1a8f6e4f4', 'word_count': 1445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7038e431-a5d5-5c7b-9467-26f1a8f6e4f4'}, {'abstract': 'It wasn’t until Dec. 11 that Franklin D. Roosevelt was able to cast aside American isolationism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/10/opinion/sunday/which-date-should-live-in-infamy.html', 'snippet': 'It wasn’t until Dec. 11 that Franklin D. Roosevelt was able to cast aside American isolationism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Winston Churchill was ebullient; he thought it was all over at last. On the evening of Sunday, Dec. 7, 1941, hosting a small birthday dinner at Chequers, the prime minister’s country retreat, for Kathleen Harriman, the daughter of the American diplomat W. Averell Harriman, Churchill heard the news of the Japanese attack on Pearl Harbor from the BBC. “At this very moment I knew the United States was in the war, up to the neck and in to the death,” he wrote in his war memoirs. “So we had won after all!” After standing alone against Berlin since the German invasion of Poland on the first day of September 1939, struggling to engage an isolationist America, Churchill “slept the sleep of the saved and thankful.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/opinion/sunday/16Greenberg-03/11MEACHAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 478, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/16/opinion/sunday/16Greenberg-03/11MEACHAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 478}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/opinion/sunday/16Greenberg-03/11MEACHAM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 816, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/opinion/sunday/16Greenberg-03/11MEACHAM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1633, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/opinion/sunday/16Greenberg-03/11MEACHAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/16/opinion/sunday/16Greenberg-03/11MEACHAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/opinion/sunday/16Greenberg-03/11MEACHAM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thu