-and-finds-the-future.html', 'snippet': 'This Warren Ellis novel about a sanitarium of futurologists is efficient and alive, but at times clichéd.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some writers have been thinking about the future for so long that now it is the future. Warren Ellis, the author of a smart, tight, occasionally tiresome new novel called “Normal,” has been at work on the subject since the early 1990s and may have decided it was time to offer a sly acknowledgment of his own longevity: The book is about a sanitarium full of futurologists in various states of nervous breakdown.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/12/arts/12BOOKELLIS2/12BOOKELLIS2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/12/arts/12BOOKELLIS2/12BOOKELLIS2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/12/arts/12BOOKELLIS2/12BOOKELLIS2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/12/arts/12BOOKELLIS2/12BOOKWARREN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/12/arts/12BOOKELLIS2/12BOOKWARREN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/12/arts/12BOOKELLIS2/12BOOKWARREN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None