aabc36-cbfb-5e81-96ea-a630cd426af3'}, {'abstract': 'For the NASA alumni and other Floridians in Patrick Ryan’s short-story collection, the American dream proves elusive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/12/books/the-dream-life-of-astronauts-patrick-ryan.html', 'snippet': 'For the NASA alumni and other Floridians in Patrick Ryan’s short-story collection, the American dream proves elusive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The stories by Patrick Ryan in “The Dream Life of Astronauts” take place in and around Cape Canaveral, Fla. Some of his characters work for NASA — or did, before they fell back into the slipstream of ordinary life. Some simply live nearby on Merritt Island, where they can watch shuttle launches from their backyards. One man, who helped double- and triple-check the thermal tiles on the doomed orbiter Challenger, feels rattled for a long time after the 1986 disaster.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/13/arts/13BOOKRYAN-jp/13BOOKRYAN-jp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/13/arts/13BOOKRYAN-jp/13BOOKRYAN-jp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/13/arts/13BOOKRYAN-jp/13BOOKRYAN-jp-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/13/arts/13BOOKRYAN-jp/13BOOKRYAN-jp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 516, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/13/arts/13BOOKRYAN-jp/13BOOKRYAN-jp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight':