RIA)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-13T09:40:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Faysal Itani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Faysal', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a45cc87-f3de-5e46-803f-ac65c80bc5b3', 'word_count': 1082, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a45cc87-f3de-5e46-803f-ac65c80bc5b3'}, {'abstract': 'The purchase of Pilsner Urquell and other Central and East European brands would give the Japanese beverage company a greater global presence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/13/business/dealbook/asahi-abinbev-beer-pilsner.html', 'snippet': 'The purchase of Pilsner Urquell and other Central and East European brands would give the Japanese beverage company a greater global presence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Asahi Group, the Japanese beer giant, said on Tuesday that it would pay $7.8 billion to buy a group of Central and Eastern European beer brands from Anheuser-Busch InBev, in the latest brand shuffle for the rapidly consolidating brewing business.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/14/world/14db-beer-1/14db-beer-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/14/world/14db-beer-1/14db-beer-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/14/world/14db-beer-1/14db-beer-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 't