s.com/2016/12/14/world/australia/trump-asia-pacific-harry-harris.html', 'snippet': '“You can count on America now and into the future,” Adm. Harry B. Harris Jr., head of the United States Pacific Command, said Wednesday in Sydney, Australia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SYDNEY, Australia — The commander of United States military operations in the Asia-Pacific region said on Wednesday that America’s commitment to the region would continue after Donald J. Trump became president, as would its opposition to Chinese expansion in the South China Sea.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Change in U.S. Commitment to Asia-Pacific Under Trump, Admiral Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Pledges to Maintain Asia-Pacific Interests', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Innis, Michelle', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Harry B Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-14T08:46:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Australia', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michelle Innis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Innis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1856442-287f-5cd5-ac87-9cf4ca15b896', 'word_count': 567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1856442-287f-5cd5-ac87-9cf4ca15b896'}, {'abstract': 'Anup Shah spends his days patiently waiting to make up-close black-and-white portraits of the lions, leopards and wildebeests of Kenya’s Masai Mara, hoping to reveal something of their personalities.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/12/14/secrets-of-wildlife-on-kenyas-masai-mara/', 'snippet': 'Anup Shah spends his days patiently waiting to make up-close black-and-white portraits of the lions, leopards and wildebeests of Kenya’s Masai Mara, hoping to reveal something of their personalities.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I just came back from seeing elephants,” Anup Shah said over the phone from Kenya on a recent Saturday. Now, for anyone else that might be the highlight of the year, if not a lifetime. But for Mr. Shah, a wildlife photographer, it was just another day. When he wakes up in a tent on Kenya’s Masai Mara National Reserve, his day begins with animals. “When the birds start calling,” he said, “I get up, and off I go just before dawn.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Secrets of Wildlife on Kenya’s Masai Mara', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Parks, Monuments and Seashores', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shah, Anup (Photographer)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-14T09:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kerri MacDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kerri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': N