ported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/dd1c4c17-8ba3-576b-b50b-fb5bf70bfe7e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/dd1c4c17-8ba3-576b-b50b-fb5bf70bfe7e'}, {'abstract': 'The radio host on talking about politics in public and whether we’ve elected a president who appears to be indifferent to religion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/14/magazine/krista-tippett-thinks-we-cant-change-one-anothers-minds.html', 'snippet': 'The radio host on talking about politics in public and whether we’ve elected a president who appears to be indifferent to religion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People say to never discuss religion or politics with others in public, but do you think that we should be talking about these topics more openly now? Coming out of this election year, I think what we absolutely have to find a way and a place and a vocabulary to talk about is moral imagination: the human effects of policies and the question of how we create common life and who we are to one another. We don’t necessarily need religious or political doctrine to answer those questions.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '66', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/magazine/18talk/18talk-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/18/magazine/18talk/18talk-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/magazine/18talk/18talk-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/magazine/18talk/18talk-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/18/magazine/18talk/18talk-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1200}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/magazine/18talk/18talk-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 512, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/magazine/18talk/18talk-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Krista Tippett Thinks We Can’t Change One Another’s Minds', 'kicker': 'Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Krista Tippett Thinks We Can’t Change One Another’s Minds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cox, Ana Marie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Public Radio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tippett, Krista', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'On Being (Radio Program)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-14T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Ana Marie Cox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Ana', 'lastname': 'Marie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/334b5bfc-3a6c-58e6-9f9f-7e940b2fa6c1', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/334b5bfc-3a6c-58e6-9f9f-7e940b2fa6c1'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on how to handle customers’ bigoted views and whether to approach your neighbors about their dog hoarding.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/14/magazine/what-should-you-do-when-customers-make-racist-remarks.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on how to handle customers’ bigoted views and whether to approach your neighbors about their dog hoarding.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I grew up in New York and moved to a small Pacific Northwest ski town a year and a half ago. I work as a bookseller-manager at an independent bookstore. I love my job, but this election cycle brought out some heated feelings.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/magazine/18ethicist/18ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/18/magazine/18ethicist/18ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/magazine/18ethicist/18ethicist-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/magazine/18ethicist/18ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1036, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/18/magazine/18ethicist/18ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1036}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/magazine/18ethicist/18ethicist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 593, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/magazine/18ethicist/18ethicist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1083, 'width': 627, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Should You Do When Customers Make Racist Remarks?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Do I Do When Customers Make Racist Remarks?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appiah, Kwame Anthony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Abuse, Rights and Welfare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicist, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-14T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4acc730-d7f3-52c1-a452-fb81795296c6', 'word_count': 1464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4acc730-d7f3-52c1-a452-fb81795296c6'}, {'abstract': 'The year 1980 brought us the greatest holiday song of all time: one that finds beauty in the shabbiness of real life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/14/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-dan-fogelberg-same-old-lang-syne.html', 'snippet': 'The year 1980 brought us the greatest holiday song of all time: one that finds beauty in the shabbiness of real life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let us resist, as another year slides darkly toward its death, the creeping fascism of holiday music. It is not normal; it is not a public good. Holiday music is sonic propaganda, crackling down at us from ancient mall sound systems and pouring point-blank from the mouths of horrible neighbors. It erodes our humanity with its cheerful clichés. Resist the elves and the messiahs, the apple-cheeked grandmothers and the man-size golems of sentient snow; resist the melodies that jump and flip like windup toys. Resist the fa and the la and the la la la. We are grown-ups. Let’s look at life, for once, full in the face.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/magazine/18lor/18lor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/18/magazine/18lor/18lor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/magazine/18lor/18lor-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/magazine/18lor/18lor-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/18/magazine/18lor/18lor-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/magazine/18lor/18lor-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width