: 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cold War Era', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-14T15:26:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73e17778-1aeb-5cf0-9157-23325160a2ca', 'word_count': 1208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73e17778-1aeb-5cf0-9157-23325160a2ca'}, {'abstract': 'This two-hour special from the Wachowskis and J. Michael Straczynski arrives on Friday, Dec. 23.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/14/arts/television/sense8-a-christmas-special-is-coming-to-netflix.html', 'snippet': 'This two-hour special from the Wachowskis and J. Michael Straczynski arrives on Friday, Dec. 23.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When last we saw the alluring, transcendentally attuned global citizens of Netflix’s “Sense8,” they were sailing into the North Atlantic on a fishing boat. But wherever they landed, trouble was sure to follow. And in “Sense8: A Christmas Special” (debuting Friday, Dec. 23) — a two-hour gift from the Wachowskis and J. Michael Straczynski, the masterminds of the series — it has. The stars are back in their own worlds, and in one another’s minds: Nomi (Jamie Clayton) hides in San Francisco; Riley (Tuppence Middleton) drugs Will (Brian J. Smith) in Amsterdam; life is upended for Lito (Miguel Ángel Silvestre) in Mexico; Sun (Doona Bae) languishes in a South Korean prison; Capheus (Toby Onwumere) tinkers with his bus in Nairobi; and Kala (Tina Desai) can’t keep Wolfgang (Max Riemelt), in Berlin, out of her marital bed in Mumbai. And the henchman Mr. Whispers (Terrence Mann) lurks. Meanwhile, there are birthdays and holidays to celebrate with raves, orgies and unconditional support — a joyful excuse to keep fans sated until Season 2 in May.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18GUIDE7/18GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18GUIDE7/18GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18GUIDE7/18GUIDE7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18GUIDE7/18GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18GUIDE7/18GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 667}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18GUIDE7/18GUIDE7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 922, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18GUIDE7/18GUIDE7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2003, 'width': 1803, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Sense8: A Christmas Special’ Is Coming to Netflix', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Television; Holiday Travels With ‘Sense8’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Web-Original Programming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Sense8 (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Netflix Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-14T15:57:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6f22aff-f420-5c97-9275-97e86309e886', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6f22aff-f420-5c97-9275-97e86309e886'}, {'abstract': 'This 100-minute English-language version is tailored to families around the holidays.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/14/arts/music/the-magic-flute-trimmed-down-at-the-metropolitan-opera.html', 'snippet': 'This 100-minute English-language version is tailored to families around the holidays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We wouldn’t want to be the ones to trim an hour of Mozart’s sublime “The Magic Flute.” But several years ago, the Metropolitan Opera took up the scissors, creating a 100-minute English-language version tailored to families around the holidays.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18GUIDE2/18GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18GUIDE2/18GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ