rganization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90306b83-b062-5ba7-9c4e-5121b093ecd2', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90306b83-b062-5ba7-9c4e-5121b093ecd2'}, {'abstract': 'His farewell concert in his hometown, New York City, will take place Dec. 21 at the Apollo Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/14/arts/music/mos-def-bids-goodbye-to-music-and-acting-at-the-apollo.html', 'snippet': 'His farewell concert in his hometown, New York City, will take place Dec. 21 at the Apollo Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yasiin Bey, the rapper best known as Mos Def, announced earlier this year that he will retire from music and acting, and he’s following through. His farewell concerts in his hometown, New York City, will take place Wednesday, Dec. 21, and Thursday at the Apollo Theater before he moves on to the Kennedy Center in Washington. The Apollo is an appropriate spot, steeped in the African-American heritage and sense of community that Mos Def’s raps have constantly invoked, both with Talib Kweli in Black Star and in diverse projects on his own. Politics, history and a sense of cultural responsibility have always informed his work, usually with a touch light enough to avoid being didactic. With luck, he’ll continue getting his message across in other media. (212-531-5300, apollotheater.org)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18GUIDE3/18GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18GUIDE3/18GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18GUIDE3/18GUIDE3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subTy