 featured already, and entertainers including Jackie Beat will perform in this monthlong series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How can you not feel holiday spirit when standing up at the Laurie Beechman Theater, swaying your arms and singing “Let There Be Peace on Earth” with the drag queen Ginger Minj? Such was my enviable lot recently, and while that show is over, the monthlong “Christmas Is a Drag” series at the Beechman continues this week with some of the most offbeat holiday entertainment you’ll find.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18GUIDE6/18GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18GUIDE6/18GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18GUIDE6/18GUIDE6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18GUIDE6/18GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 461, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18GUIDE6/18GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 461}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18GUIDE6/18GUIDE6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 786, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18GUIDE6/18GUIDE6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1573, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Christmas Is a Drag’ Dresses Up for the Holidays', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Theater; All Dressed Up for Christmas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "RuPaul's Drag Race (TV Program)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beechman, Laurie, Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-14T16:05:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven McElroy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McElroy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e8344bc-f694-58af-9771-98b26fbd26b4', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e8344bc-f694-58af-9771-98b26fbd26b4'}, {'abstract': '“The Tree of the Wooden Clogs,” Ermanno Olmi’s Palme d’Or-winning film of Italian peasant families in the late 19th century, is showing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/14/movies/the-farming-life-in-an-older-italy-at-film-forum.html', 'snippet': '“The Tree of the Wooden Clogs,” Ermanno Olmi’s Palme d’Or-winning film of Italian peasant families in the late 19th century, is showing.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Tree of Wooden Clogs,” Ermanno Olmi’s farsighted view of Italian farm life in the late 19th century, immerses you in what feels like an unchanging preindustrial world. The beautiful three-hour film, which won the Palme d’Or at Cannes in 1978, follows the lives of four peasant families laboring on the estate of an absentee landlord in the province of Bergamo. The actors, all residents of the area, speak in their native dialect.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times'