tchens-of-this-city-describes-a-syrian-hell.html', 'snippet': 'Khaled Khalifa’s episodic novel focuses on one family in Aleppo, his native city, and stops several years short of the Syrian civil war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aleppo has essentially fallen. The images have been unignorable, calamitous: of residents wandering numbly through burning city streets; of parents sobbing over dead children; of the strong wheeling away the weak. On Tuesday, a United Nations official described the massacre of fleeing civilians as “a complete meltdown of humanity.” Residents have been tweeting out their goodbyes. Tens of thousands have already been displaced or perished.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/15/arts/15BOOKKHALIFAJP/15BOOKKHALIFAJP-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/15/arts/15BOOKKHALIFAJP/15BOOKKHALIFAJP-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/15/arts/15BOOKKHALIFAJP/15BOOKKHALIFAJP-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/15/arts/15BOOKKHALIFAJP/15BOOKKHALIFAJP-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 878, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/15/arts/15BOOKKHALIFAJP/15BOOKKHALIFAJP-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 878}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/15/arts/15BOOKKHALIFAJP/15BOOKKHALIFAJP-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 700,