ract': 'Quotation of the day for Thursday, December 15, 2016.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/14/todayspaper/quotation-of-the-day.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the day for Thursday, December 15, 2016.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The whole project knows about it. The only one they’re not telling is me.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-12-15T02:21:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a02efb7-96a9-5582-af75-9ebbdd92607a', 'word_count': 36, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a02efb7-96a9-5582-af75-9ebbdd92607a'}, {'abstract': 'The people in his works often carried umbrellas and wore hats, or kissed atop taxi cabs. “I perceive my pictures as playing with time and space,” he said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/14/arts/design/rodney-smith-dead-photographer.html', 'snippet': 'The people in his works often carried umbrellas and wore hats, or kissed atop taxi cabs. “I perceive my pictures as playing with time and space,” he said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rodney Smith, a prominent photographer whose whimsical work invited comparisons to that of the Belgian surrealist René Magritte’s, died on Dec. 5 at his home in Snedens Landing, N.Y. He was 68.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rodney Smith, Whimsical Photographer, Dies at 68', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rodney Smith, 68, Photographer of Surrealistic Whimsy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Rodney Lewis (1947-2016)', '