cle/be3c8258-3683-54bd-81c1-ab34d1f7c4dd'}, {'abstract': 'Ken Hechler, who died at 102, served in Congress and also as a professor, state official, speechwriter and novelist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/15/opinion/coal-miners-lose-their-appalachian-champion.html', 'snippet': 'Ken Hechler, who died at 102, served in Congress and also as a professor, state official, speechwriter and novelist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ken Hechler was an extraordinary, long-lived politician who arrived fresh from the New Deal in the coal hollows of West Virginia six decades ago as a carpetbagger from New York. He soon became the ultimate antagonist of Big Coal for its neglect and abuse of miners, serving as their voice in Congress for nine terms.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/15/opinion/15thu3web/15thu3web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/15/opinion/15thu3web/15thu3web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/15/opinion/15thu3web/15thu3web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/15/opinion/15thu3web/15thu3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 344, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/15/opinion/15thu3web/15thu3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 344}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/15/opinion/15thu3web/15thu3web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 588