ential Election of 2016', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-15T19:32:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Hirschfeld Davis and David E. Sanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': 'Hirschfeld', 'lastname': 'Davis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Sanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0806a30-0533-55ae-b75c-4e36dd8a460f', 'word_count': 1227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0806a30-0533-55ae-b75c-4e36dd8a460f'}, {'abstract': 'The investors behind the Kraft-Heinz merger may be looking for more deals, with Mondelez International and other companies potentially up for grabs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/15/business/dealbook/3g-capital-is-expected-to-be-in-a-buying-mood-in-2017.html', 'snippet': 'The investors behind the Kraft-Heinz merger may be looking for more deals, with Mondelez International and other companies potentially up for grabs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Brazilian billionaires at 3G Capital that turned Kraft Heinz and Anheuser-Busch InBev into mega-acquisition machines will dive back into the buying business in the coming year. Their next target should be Mondelez International, the $66 billion food conglomerate that failed to coax the chocolate maker Hershey into a sale in 2016. A deal will require some unusual ingredients.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '3G Capital Is Expected to Be in a Buying Mood in 2017', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kraft Heinz Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '3G Capital Management LLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mondelez International Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-15T19:39:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Allison', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allison', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abd192fd-769f-59cb-b02a-e8e421cd70a7', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abd192fd-769f-59cb-b02a-e8e421cd70a7'}, {'abstract': 'Girl at the White Horse, which opens this month, has a series of cozy and intimate nooks to hang out in.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/15/t-magazine/cocktails-los-angeles-girl-at-the-white-horse.html', 'snippet': 'Girl at the White Horse, which opens this month, has a series of cozy and intimate nooks to hang out in.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reza Fahim designed Tenants of the Trees, a nightclub in the Silver Lake neighborhood of Los Angeles, for the new generation of Hollywood stars that relishes privacy: It’s surrounded by 14-foot high concrete walls. Within the cramped, labyrinthine corridors of Tenants, on the smallest dance floor in Los Angeles, Frank Ocean swayed incognito on the night his long-anticipated second album, “Blonde,” dropped last August. And on a recent Thursday night, the burgeoning London rockers the Big Moon claimed a cabaret stage to play a secret concert to close their first North American tour; unbeknown to them, the band served as an opening act for an impromptu two-hour set by Dave Chappelle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/15/t-magazine/15tmag-whitehorse01/15tmag-whitehorse01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/15/t-magazine/15tmag-whitehorse01/15tmag-whitehorse01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/15/t-magazine/15tmag-whitehorse01/15tmag-whitehorse01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/15/t-magazine/15tmag-whitehorse01/15tmag-whitehorse01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/15/t-magazine/15tmag-whitehorse01/15tmag-whitehorse01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/15/t-magazine/15tmag-whitehorse01/15tmag-whitehorse01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/15/t-magazine/15tmag-whitehorse01/15tmag-whitehorse01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Like Drinking Cocktails at Home, in L.A.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-12-15T19:46:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Robb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dde1d67b-e070-53b9-8cca-3fab3eba10e3', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dde1d67b-e070-53b9-8cca-3fab3eba10e3'}, {'abstract': 'Also: When you realize you didn’t get an invitation to a holiday party you’ve gone to for years; the complexities of gift giving, and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/15/fashion/social-qs-advice-family-visit-hotel-holiday-party-invitation-gift-giving.html', 'snippet': 'Also: When you realize you didn’t get an invitation to a holiday party you’ve gone to for years; the complexities of gift giving, and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am 55 and the oldest of four siblings. We all congregate at our parents’ home (with spouses and kids) over the holidays. Their place has many bedrooms but only two baths. The commotion is fun during the day, but at night, the house is overcrowded and noisy. For a few years, I have gotten a hotel room three blocks away. I only use it for sleeping and showering. But sleeping there, instead of on the couch, causes resentment in the family, especially from my mother. How can I explain that I don’t mean offense?', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, '