, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/16/us/16jewel1_xp/16jewel1_xp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/16/us/16jewel1_xp/16jewel1_xp-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/16/us/16jewel1_xp/16jewel1_xp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/16/us/16jewel1_xp/16jewel1_xp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/16/us/16jewel1_xp/16jewel1_xp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/16/us/16jewel1_xp/16jewel1_xp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1639, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Retirement for a Jewel Thief With a Seven-Decade Career', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Payne, Doris (1930- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dunwoody (Ga)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-15T21:29:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonah Engel Bromwich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonah', 'middlename': 'Engel', 'lastname': 'Bromwich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4314eebe-edf1-55fb-9240-726bc24a4ca7', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4314eebe-edf1-55fb-9240-726bc24a4ca7'}, {'abstract': 'Cheng Er’s gangland drama unwinds nonchronologically, like episodes of a mini-series shown out of order.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/15/movies/the-wasted-times-review.html', 'snippet': 'Cheng Er’s gangland drama unwinds nonchronologically, like episodes of a mini-series shown out of order.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Set against the backdrop of the second Sino-Japanese War, “The Wasted Times” has the outward appearance of being a sweeping gangland epic. But by employing a nonlinear structure, Cheng Er — who wrote, directed and edited this film — severely diffuses the story’s dramatic impact. To think back through the narrative, which spans more than a decade, is to wonder what was gained by withholding details only to reveal them later in flashbacks.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘The Wasted Times,’ a Hopscotching Shanghai Crime Tale', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Wasted Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Wasted Times (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cheng Er', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-15T21:40:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Kenigsberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenigsberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/342cb076-7000-5322-adb2-de7c0cb0007b', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/342cb076-7000-5322-adb2-de7c0cb0007b'}, {'abstract': 'New York Times critics pick their favorite movies of the year, with links telling you where to stream them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/15/watching/best-movies-of-2016-where-to-watch.html', 'snippet': 'New York Times critics pick their favorite movies of the year, with links telling you where to stream them.', 'lead_paragraph': '‘Tis the season for big family films and Oscar hopefuls. But as the film critics for The New York Times remind us, there were plenty of great movies that opened in the year’s other 11 months. If you happened to miss any, their lists of the best movies of the year should help.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/22/watching/embrace-the-serpent-watching/22watching4-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 294, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/07/22/watching/embrace-the-serpent-watching/22watching4-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 294}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/22/watching/embrace-the-serpent-watching/22watching4-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 501, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/22/watching/embrace-the-serpent-watching/22watching4-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1002, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/22/watching/embrace-the-serpent-watching/embrace-the-serpent-watching-thumbStandard-v9.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/07/22/watching/embrace-the-serpent-watching/embrace-the-serpent-watching-thumbStandard-v9.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/22/watching/embrace-the-serpent-watching/22watching4-thumbLarge-v6.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where to Stream the Best Movies of 2016', 'kicker': 'Watch This', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-15T21:43:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Watching', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Castillo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castillo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2ad0140-0ca1-5533-9362-085a90e883f8', 'word_count': 830, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2ad0140-0ca1-5533-9362-085a90e883f8'}, {'abstract': 'The actress plays multiple roles in Julian Rosefeldt’s ‘Manifesto’ video installation at the Park Avenue Armory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/15/arts/design/12-faces-of-cate-blanchett-a-chameleon-in-the-armory.html', 'snippet': 'The actress plays multiple roles in Julian Rosefeldt’s ‘Manifesto’ video installation at the Park Avenue Armory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the art world gave out Oscars, Cate Blanchett should win for her tour de force of starring roles in “Manifesto,” at the Park Avenue Armory. This toweringly ambitious, if occasionally pretentious film installation is the creation of Julian Rosefeldt, its writer, director and producer, a German artist drawn to complex narratives and fusions of real and cinematic space. His latest effort consists of 13 short films whose scripts are stitched together from nearly 50 manifestoes mostly by 20th-century artists, composers, architects and filmmakers. From Futurism to Pop Art and beyond, the writings layer knowledge, language and style into head-spinning densities. Some of these treatises were important turning points in art history; others are nearly forgotten.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/16/arts/16MANIFESTO1/16MANIFESTO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/16/arts/16MANIFESTO1/16MANIFESTO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/16/arts/16MANIFESTO1/16MANIFESTO1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/16/arts/16MANIFESTO1/16MANIFESTO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 234, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/16/arts/16MANIFESTO1/16MANIFESTO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 234}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/16/arts/16MANIFESTO1/16MANIFESTO1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/16/arts/16MANIFESTO1/16MANIFESTO1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 798, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '12 Faces of Cate Blanchett: A Chameleon in the Armory', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '12 Faces of Cate: The Chameleon in the Armory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosefeldt, Julian (1965- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blanchett, Cate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Manifesto (Exhibit)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Park Avenue Armory (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-15T21:49:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1eea528e-ea17-54e7-9241-b7b4bc342dd8', 'word_count': 1131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1eea528e-ea17-54e7-9241-b7b4bc342dd8'}, {'abstract': 'Kim Nguyen’s film focuses on a pair of damaged young souls enveloped in beauty, absurdity and, despite the cold air, a lot of overheated romanticism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/15/movies/two-lovers-and-a-bear-review.html', 'snippet': 'Kim Nguyen’s film focuses on a pair of damaged young souls enveloped in beauty, absurdity and, despite the cold air, a lot of overheated romanticism.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Two Lovers and a Bear” begins with two-thirds of the title characters — the lovers — sledding to a frozen body of water, where they then drill holes and do some 