: 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9de1b472-b11e-5cc9-a1ee-492ee3165121', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9de1b472-b11e-5cc9-a1ee-492ee3165121'}, {'abstract': '“Adventures in Moominland,” in London, exhibits (and celebrates) the cult midcentury cartoonist Tove Jansson’s Moomin series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/15/t-magazine/art/moomin-tove-jansson-adventures-moominland.html', 'snippet': '“Adventures in Moominland,” in London, exhibits (and celebrates) the cult midcentury cartoonist Tove Jansson’s Moomin series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During her lifetime, the artist, author and cartoonist Tove Jansson earned fame far beyond her native Finland for her children’s books featuring the Moomins, a race of hippo-like, bulbous-nosed creatures driven by abundant curiosity. Their intrepid exploits, as well as Jansson’s formidable inventiveness, inform the spirit of the exhibition “Adventures in Moominland,” which opens tomorrow at London’s Southbank Centre.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beloved Children’s-Book Characters, in Their Own Immersive World', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southbank Centre (London, England)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Finland', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-15T22:14:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hettie Judah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hettie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Judah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eddac597-0a7d-57a0-90a4-1a19c1140d12', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eddac597-0a7d-57a0-90a4-1a19c1140d12'}, {'abstract': 'Circus der Sinne, based in Tanzania, deploys performers who leap, juggle and perform myriad other feats at the New Victory Theater, backed by a live band.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/15/theater/review-mother-africa-my-home-melds-acrobatics-and-drumming.html', 'snippet': 'Circus der Sinne, based in Tanzania, deploys performers who leap, juggle and perform myriad other feats at the New Victory Theater, backed by a live band.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Life may hold no guarantees, but unless the roof falls in at the New Victory Theater, you’re pretty much assured a swell time at “Mother Africa: My Home.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/19/arts/19MOTHERAFRICA/16MOTHERAFRICA1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/19/arts/19MOTHERAFRICA/16MOTHERAFRICA1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/19/arts/19MOTHERAFRICA/16MOTHERAFRICA1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/19/arts/19MOTHERAFRICA/16MOTHERAFRICA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/19/arts/19MOTHERAFRICA/16MOTHERAFRICA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0