'uri': 'nyt://article/cd4c0e5a-7cf2-5beb-a8e5-86f6dc74623d'}, {'abstract': 'A woman fleeing Aleppo, Syria, goes unmentioned in a caption, but not unnoticed by readers. And a student’s violent threat appears to be equated in severity with criticism of racism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/16/public-editor/friday-mailbag-the-veil-storm-troopers-and-false-equivalence.html', 'snippet': 'A woman fleeing Aleppo, Syria, goes unmentioned in a caption, but not unnoticed by readers. And a student’s violent threat appears to be equated in severity with criticism of racism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, the mailbag has gone international. We’ll begin in Aleppo, where a pro-Syrian government offensive was forcing civilians to flee. The Times captured the ongoing escape with the lead photo of the Dec. 13 issue carrying the caption: “A man fleeing to rebel-held areas of Aleppo, Syria, on Monday, carrying a child with an IV drip.” Readers took issue with the fact that the caption did not note the woman in the photo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/17pubedmail/17pubedmail-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/17pubedmail/17pubedmail-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/17pubedmail/17pubedmail-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/17pubedmail/17pubedmail-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 454, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016