ng 40, made iconic scenes in movie history possible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After scouting locations for “Rocky,” the director John G. Avildsen still had no idea how to pull off a crucial scene. Then his assistant cameraman invited him to view a demonstration reel for a new piece of equipment. It included a shot of the inventor’s girlfriend running up the stairs of the Philadelphia Museum of Art. “And I said, ‘Hmm, I know just where that’s going to go,’” Mr. Avildsen recalled.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18STEADICAM2SUB/18STEADICAM2SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18STEADICAM2SUB/18STEADICAM2SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18STEADICAM2SUB/18STEADICAM2SUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18STEADICAM2SUB/18STEADICAM2SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 324, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18STEADICAM2SUB/18STEADICAM2SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 324}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18STEADICAM2SUB/18STEADICAM2SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 554, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/arts/18STEADICAM2SUB/18STEAD