ow’ Correspondent Adjusts to Life in New York', 'kicker': 'What I Love', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finding Niceties in Cramped Quarters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Minhaj, Hasan (1985- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': "Hell's Kitchen (Manhattan, NY)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Hasan Minhaj: Homecoming King (Play)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Daily Show with Trevor Noah (TV Program)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-16T20:52:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c07d069a-69fd-51f4-99db-e5f18601bd3d', 'word_count': 823, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c07d069a-69fd-51f4-99db-e5f18601bd3d'}, {'abstract': 'Sooner or later, we all return to the highest honor our nation bestows: being a good citizen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/16/opinion/the-humiliations-of-life-after-congress.html', 'snippet': 'Sooner or later, we all return to the highest honor our nation bestows: being a good citizen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Washington — Once, I occupied a prized office in the Rayburn House Office Building, with a commanding view that stretched to the Lincoln Memorial. Now, I occupy Cubicle No. 45, with a decent view of Cubicles 44 and 46.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/17israelWeb/17israelWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/17israelWeb/17israelWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/17israelWeb/17israelWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/17israelWeb/17israelWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/17israelWeb/17israelWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/17israelWeb/17israelWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/17israelWeb/17israelWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Humiliations of Life After Congress', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Humiliations of Life After Congress', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Israel, Steve J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-16T20:53:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Israel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Israel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/79b53260-9a3a-55a8-a927-247b4b954aa3', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79b53260-9a3a-55a8-a927-247b4b954aa3'}, {'abstract': 'The selection of David Friedman, a bankruptcy lawyer with extremist views, is a serious mistake.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/16/opinion/donald-trumps-israel-ambassador-pick-is-hazardous-to-peace.html', 'snippet': 'The selection of David Friedman, a bankruptcy lawyer with extremist views, is a serious mistake.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PRINCETON, N.J. — President-elect Donald J. Trump’s selection of David Friedman as United States ambassador to Israel is a serious mistake that should be rectified. Spoken and published statements by Mr. Friedman, a 57-year-old bankruptcy lawyer in New York, about Israel and American policies in the Mideast suggest he is unsuitable to represent America in one of the most high-pressure diplomatic positions in the world. This call to withdraw Mr. Friedman’s name also reflects a sober assessment of the damage that could be caused to American interests and to Mr. Trump’s presidency by the reckless words for which Mr. Friedman is already known.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/16kurtzerWeb/16kurtzerWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/16kurtzerWeb/16kurtzerWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/16kurtzerWeb/16kurtzerWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/16kurtzerWeb/16kurtzerWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/16kurtzerWeb/16kurtzerWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 411}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/16kurtzerWeb/16kurtzerWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/16kurtzerWeb/16kurtzerWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1404, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Donald Trump’s Israel Ambassador Pick Is Hazardous to Peace', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Our Man in Tel Aviv', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedman, David M (1958- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-16T21:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel C. Kurtzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Kurtzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/216143df-a326-5d4f-bf84-8e2a5f074a00', 'word_count': 769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/216143df-a326-5d4f-bf84-8e2a5f074a00'}, {'abstract': 'The president said he refrained from retaliating against Moscow for hacking the D.N.C. before the election because he did not want it to be seen as unfair meddling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/16/us/politics/obama-putin-hacking-news-conference.html', 'snippet': 'The president said he refrained from retaliating against Moscow for hacking the D.N.C. before the election because he did not want it to be seen as unfair meddling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama said for the first time on Friday that he had held back from retaliating against Russia’s meddling in the presidential race for fear of inciting further hacking “that could hamper vote counting.” But he said he was weighing a mix of public and covert actions against the Russians in his last 34 days in office, actions that would increase “the costs for them.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Says He Told Putin: ‘Cut It Out’ on Hacking', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Defends Muted Response to Russian Hacks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landler, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'C