s High School, Rosemarie Jahoda, whom they want removed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Townsend Harris High School is one of New York City’s most prestigious public schools, where 100 percent of students graduate on time and all of them are prepared for college, according to city metrics.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Elite Queens High School, PTA Calls Embattled Principal ‘Rude’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Elite Queens High School, PTA Denounces Principal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jahoda, Rosemarie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Townsend Harris High School', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Principals (School)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parent-Teacher Associations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-17T02:25:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/016786a3-f776-5f7e-9c7e-ab231cb3e86d', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/016786a3-f776-5f7e-9c7e-ab231cb3e86d'}, {'abstract': 'Riding the Iron Curtain Trail in winter probably makes one an epic fool, not an epic hero. But I had to believe otherwise.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/16/opinion/6000-miles-on-a-shopping-bike.html', 'snippet': 'Riding the Iron Curtain Trail in winter probably makes one an epic fool, not an epic hero. But I had to believe otherwise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'London — Every bike ride is a pocket drama. Reflect on the humblest cycling commute and you’ll find yourself reliving short-story excitements denied to co-workers who yawned their way in on the train: the reconstructive surgery so skilfully swerved when some idiot flung open his car door, the race you pretended not to have with that courier, those bracing exchanges with bike-blind jaywalkers and cabdrivers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/17mooreWeb/17mooreWeb-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/17mooreWeb/17mooreWeb-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/17mooreWeb/17mooreWeb-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/17mooreWeb/17sportingWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/17mooreWeb/17sportingWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/17mooreWeb/17sportingWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/17/opinion/17mooreWeb/17sportingWeb-superJumbo.jpg