ps://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/17/opinion/sunday/future-aleppo-mohammed-qutaish.html', 'snippet': 'A young artist recreates the city he remembered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mohammed Qutaish, who was born in Aleppo, was 10 when popular protests broke out against President, Bashar al-Assad of Syria. “I wasn’t sure exactly what was going on but I liked it. It felt positive,” Mohammed told me during one of our video-chats earlier this year. However, protesters were met with force, violence escalated and soon Mohammed and his family fled their beloved city. When they returned four months later, having been told that it was safely under the control of opposition forces, they were shocked to see the city in ruins.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/18opart1/18opart1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/18opart1/18opart1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/18opart1/18opart1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/18opart1/18opart1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 283, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/18opart1/18opart1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 283}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/18opart1/18opart1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 483, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtyp