terial': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf4fb3a2-09c2-5536-8a15-dee5226fdb38', 'word_count': 9, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf4fb3a2-09c2-5536-8a15-dee5226fdb38'}, {'abstract': 'Vladimir Putin is being rewarded for his attack on the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/17/opinion/sunday/donald-trump-the-russian-poodle.html', 'snippet': 'Vladimir Putin is being rewarded for his attack on the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1972, President Richard Nixon’s White House dispatched burglars to bug Democratic Party offices. That Watergate burglary and related “dirty tricks,” such as releasing mice at a Democratic press conference and paying a woman to strip naked and shout her love for a Democratic candidate, nauseated Americans — and impelled some of us kids at the time to pursue journalism.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18kristof-web/18kristof-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18kristof-web/18kristof-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18kristof-web/18kristof-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18kristof-web/18kristof-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 428, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18kristof-web/18kristof-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 428}}, {'rank': 0, '