nted chief strategist for President-elect Donald J. Trump, profiles noted that he was a co-author of a rap musical based on Shakespeare’s Roman tragedy “Coriolanus.” The revelation played as a punch line, another loopy swerve in a career that took Mr. Bannon from a working-class Democratic family to the Trump White House. Coming just after Mr. Trump denounced the hip-hop hit “Hamilton” as “overrated,” the news that his right-hand man had scripted a hip-hop statesman himself felt almost comical.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18Pollack-Pelzner/18Pollack-Pelzner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18Pollack-Pelzner/18Pollack-Pelzner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18Pollack-Pelzner/18Pollack-Pelzner-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18Pollack-Pelzner/18Pollack-Pelzner-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 532, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18Pollack-Pelzner/18Pollack-Pelzner-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 532}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18Pollack-Pelzner/18Pollack-Pelzner-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 907, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18Pollack-Pelzner/18Pollack-Pelzner-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 918, 'width': 1036, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Behold, Steve Bannon’s Hip-Hop Shakespeare Rewrite: ‘Coriolanus’', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bannon’s ‘Coriolanus’ Rewrite', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bannon, Stephen K', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pollack-Pelzner, Daniel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Coriolanus (Play)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-17T19:30:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Pollack-Pelzner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack-Pelzner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/61299819-1699-54e0-80fd-caf3ffcc5b4b', 'word_count': 955, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61299819-1699-54e0-80fd-caf3ffcc5b4b'}, {'abstract': 'My co-workers had uncertain futures, and no easy explanation for why the American dream didn’t work out for them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/17/opinion/sunday/white-resentment-on-the-night-shift-at-walmart.html', 'snippet': 'My co-workers had uncertain futures, and no easy explanation for why the American dream didn’t work out for them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seven years ago, I joined the night shift at a Walmart in rural Michigan. For $8.10 an hour, I spent four or five nights a week filling shelves with the flour and sugar and marshmallow fluff that residents of the local county, which in 2008 voted for Barack Obama, needed to get through the holidays. Four years ago, the county went with President Obama a second time, though by a thinner margin. But this past November, the county, like the state, turned red.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18mcmillan/18mcmillan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18mcmillan/18mcmillan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18mcmillan/18mcmillan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18mcmillan/18mcmillan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18mcmillan/18mcmillan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18mcmillan/18mcmillan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18mcmillan/18mcmillan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1358, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'White Resentment on the Night Shift at Walmart', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'White Resentment on the Night Shift at Walmart', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McMillan, Tracie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whites', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walmart Stores Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-17T19:30:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tracie McMillan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tracie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McMillan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/688c1bd9-f29c-5364-9c6a-6d9010a06664', 'word_count': 1168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/688c1bd9-f29c-5364-9c6a-6d9010a06664'}, {'abstract': 'The case for political moderation in our immoderate age.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/17/opinion/sunday/one-way-not-to-be-like-trump.html', 'snippet': 'The case for political moderation in our immoderate age.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE Trump era will be unpredictable in many ways. But there’s one thing that we can reasonably count on. Moderation, an ancient virtue, will be viewed with contempt. After all, the most temperamentally immoderate major party nominee in American history ran for president and won because of it. Victory spawns imitation, and the Trump template is likely to influence our politics for some time to come.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/16/opinion/Wehner-Peter-circular/Wehner-Peter-circular-articleLarge-v3.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/03/16/opinion/Wehner-Peter-circular/Wehner-Peter-circular-articleLarge-v3.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/16/opinion/Wehner-Peter-circular/Wehner-Peter-circular-jumbo-v3.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/16/opinion/Wehner-Peter-circular/Wehner-Peter-circular-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/16/opinion/Wehner-Peter-circular/Wehner-Peter-circular-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/03/16/opinion/Wehner-Peter-circular/Wehner-Peter-circular-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/16/opinion/Wehner-Peter-circular/Wehner-Peter-circular-thumbLarge-v3.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Way Not to Be Like Trump', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Moderate Is Not a Dirty Word', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wehner, Peter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sartre, Jean-Paul', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARON, RAYMOND', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-17T19:30:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Wehner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wehner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8282956-2e60-5ade-83d3-debd7139ff9d', 'word_count': 934, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8282956-2e60-5ade-83d3-debd7139ff9d'}, {'abstract': 'The unifying force in the United States is whiteness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/17/opinion/sunday/what-donald-trump-doesnt-know-about-black-people.html', 'snippet': 'The unifying force in the United States is whiteness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2005, after Hurricane Katrina, Kanye West appeared on live TV during a celebrity fund-raiser for victims of the disaster and said, “George Bush doesn’t care about black people.” This wasn’t based on intimate knowledge of Mr. Bush’s racial views, but rather on his treatment of black people in a time of crisis.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18dyson/18dyson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18dyson/18dyson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18dyson/18dyson-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18dyson/18dyson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18dyson/18dyson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18dyson/18dyson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18dyson/18dyson-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1381, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Donald Trump Doesn’t Know About Black People', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Donald Trump’s Racial Ignorance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dyson, Michael Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carson, Benjamin S', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sessions, Jefferson B III', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whites', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-17T19:30:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Eric Dyson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'Eric', 'lastname': 'Dyson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d919175e-fb60-5072-bb58-d74a40713a37', 'word_count': 1376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d919175e-fb60-5072-bb58-d74a40713a37'}, {'abstract': 'They responded to years in confinement by rapidly assimilating into American culture — and supporting the president-elect.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/17/opinion/sunday/my-family-was-interned-now-theyre-with-trump.html', 'snippet': 'They responded to years in confinement by rapidly assimilating into American culture — and supporting the president-elect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was growing up my family simply called it “camp,” like the summer retreat I would escape to as a kid. Both places tended to have wood cabins, tight rows of beds and a large mess hall. My grandmother, or Baachan as I called her, used to say the baseball diamonds at her camp would draw huge crowds for every game.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18sakuma-web/18sakuma-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 464, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18sakuma-web/18sakuma-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 464}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18sakuma-web/18sakuma-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 791, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18sakuma-web/18sakuma-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1583, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18sakuma-web/18sakuma-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18sakuma-web/18sakuma-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/opinion/sunday/18sakuma-web/18sakuma-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Family Was Interned. Now They’re With Trump.', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Patriotism of Time at ‘Camp’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japanese-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II