inal': 'By Robert D. McFadden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/f212f181-401b-590c-a878-7ad8ed2e0964', 'word_count': 1814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f212f181-401b-590c-a878-7ad8ed2e0964'}, {'abstract': 'The president has vowed to “send a clear message” to Russia over its hacking of the U.S. election but has few ideal options.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/17/us/politics/obama-putin-russia-hacking-us-elections.html', 'snippet': 'The president has vowed to “send a clear message” to Russia over its hacking of the U.S. election but has few ideal options.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Over the past four months, American intelligence agencies and aides to President Obama assembled a menu of options to respond to Russia’s hacking during the election, ranging from the obvious — exposing President Vladimir V. Putin’s financial ties to oligarchs — to the innovative, including manipulating the computer code that Russia uses in designing its cyberweapons.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/us/18HACK/18HACK-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/18/us/18HACK/18HACK-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/us/18HACK/18HACK-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/18/us/18HAC