Raymond Blanc. Born in France and self taught, he opened the Manoir in Great Milton in 1984, and has used its 27 acres to grow fresh vegetables, berries and herbs for his kitchen. Over time, Mr. Blanc’s cooking, which has earned two Michelin stars, has evolved, with a broader, global palette of seasonings. But what makes this beautifully illustrated volume more than just a gift-worthy showpiece is that many of the recipes should inspire a home cook. Try chicken with morels, asparagus with chervil, salmon with spinach and watercress, poached egg on tomato fondue, Jerusalem artichoke soup, hake Grenobloise, and more: “Le Manoir aux Quat’Saisons: The Story of a Modern Classic” by Raymond Blanc (Bloomsbury, $75).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/21/dining/21BURNER-BOOK/21BURNER-BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/21/dining/21BURNER-BOOK/21BURNER-BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/21/dining/21BURNER-BOOK/21BURNER-BOOK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/21/dining/21BURNER-BOOK/21BURNER-BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 358, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/21/dining/21BURNER-BOOK/21BURNER-BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 358}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/21/dining/21BURNER-BOOK/21BURNER-BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/21/dining/21BURNER-BOOK/21BURNER-BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1222, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A French Cookbook From the English Countryside', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Persue: A Book to Impress or Perhaps Inspire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blanc, Raymond', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Le Manoir aux Quat'Saisons: The Story of a Modern Classic (Book)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-19T20:59:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/006f2128-5901-5224-8899-bd49d8ac2171', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/006f2128-5901-5224-8899-bd49d8ac2171'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Machado was the first nonwhite supermodel, and it’s a legacy the fashion industry has to wrestle with.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/19/fashion/china-machado-first-non-white-supermodel.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Machado was the first nonwhite supermodel, and it’s a legacy the fashion industry has to wrestle with.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China Machado, one of the first non-Caucasians to appear in the pages of an American glossy fashion magazine and a model who helped break not only the race barrier but also the age barrier, died on Sunday in Brookhaven, N.Y., on Long