n and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Harper's Bazaar", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'IMG Worldwide', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Avedon, Richard', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-19T21:05:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vanessa Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vanessa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d5cffea-24b9-5a88-91d7-4c6cbca96dcd', 'word_count': 1283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d5cffea-24b9-5a88-91d7-4c6cbca96dcd'}, {'abstract': 'The Kitano hotel plans an Osechi meal of foods thought to bring good fortune for the new year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/19/dining/new-years-day-osechi-japanese-meal-hakubai.html', 'snippet': 'The Kitano hotel plans an Osechi meal of foods thought to bring good fortune for the new year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To call on the new for the new year, try a restaurant feast that is traditional in Japan but uncommon in the United States. Osechi is a six-course menu of foods thought to bring good luck, good health and all of that. At Hakubai in the Kitano Hotel New York, the meal includes symbolic foods like white and red fish cakes for purity and to protect against evil, and herring roe for fertility, along with sashimi and Wagyu beef. The brunch is served on Jan. 1 and 2, with seatings throughout the day starting at 10:30 a.m., $200 per person. Reservations are required. Free sake will be served in the lobby on Jan. 1: Hakubai, 66 Park Avenue (38th Street), 212-885-7111, kitano.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/21/dining/21BURNER-BRUNCH/21BURNER-BRUNCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/21/dining/21BURNER-BRUNCH/21BURNER-BRUNCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/21/dining/21BURNER-BRUNCH/21BURNER-BRUNCH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/21/dining/21BURNER-BRUNCH/21BURNER-BRUNCH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 522, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/21/dining/21BURNER-BRUNCH/21BURNER-BRUNCH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 522}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/21/dining/21BURNER-BRUNCH/21BURNER-BRUNCH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 891, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/21/dining/21BURNER-BRUNCH/21BURNER-BRUNCH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1741, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Good Luck, Served in 6 Courses, on New Year’s Day', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Welcome: A Japanese Celebration  for a New Year’s Twist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name'