e of western Aleppo Province, on Monday, along with thousands of others displaced from the city they called home.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bana al-Abed, Child Who Became Aleppo’s Civilian Face, Is Evacuated', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Al-Abed, Bana', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evacuations and Evacuees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALEPPO (SYRIA)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-19T22:56:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Megan Specia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Megan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Specia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea969029-43c8-53a5-a759-8f235ac9c543', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea969029-43c8-53a5-a759-8f235ac9c543'}, {'abstract': 'The illustrator Edward Gorey proves a complex subject in this imagined memoir for the stage that focuses more on the man than his art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/19/theater/review-peering-behind-the-whimsically-ghoulish-gorey.html', 'snippet': 'The illustrator Edward Gorey proves a complex subject in this imagined memoir for the stage that focuses more on the man than his art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s usually wise to avoid assumptions based on an artist’s work. Actors so convincing as violent psychos go home to minivans and soccer lessons. Gilbert & George’s paintings can be provocatively outré, but they live routine lives in their conservative suits.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit'