ation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-20T08:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Desmond Lachman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Desmond', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lachman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f0a99fe-34de-5be9-abc9-e226e79b4276', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f0a99fe-34de-5be9-abc9-e226e79b4276'}, {'abstract': 'Should Zionist goals be pursued to the point of tolerating anti-Semitism?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/20/opinion/liberal-zionism-in-the-age-of-trump.html', 'snippet': 'Should Zionist goals be pursued to the point of tolerating anti-Semitism?', 'lead_paragraph': 'For weeks now, Jewish communities across America have been troubled by an awkward phenomenon. Donald J. Trump, a ruthless politician trafficking in anti-Semitic tropes, has been elected to become the next president, and he has appointed as his chief strategist Stephen K. Bannon, a prominent figure of the “alt-right,” a movement that promotes white nationalism, anti-Semitism, racism and misogyny. Though Bannon himself has expressed “zero tolerance” for such views, his past actions suggest otherwise; as the executive chairman of Breitbart News for the past four years, he provided the country’s most powerful media platform for the movement and its ideologies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/20/opinion/20stoneSub/20stoneSub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/20/opinion/20stoneSub/20stoneSub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/20/opinion/20stoneSub/20stoneSub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/20/opinion/20stoneSub/20stoneSub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/20/opinion/20stoneSub/20stoneSub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/20/opinion/20stoneSub/20stoneSub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/20/opinion/20stoneSub/20stoneSub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Liberal Zionism in the Age of Trump', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zionism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fringe Groups and Movements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liberalism (US Politics)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bannon, Stephen K', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Breitbart News Network LLC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-20T08:21:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Omri Boehm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Omri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Boehm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae6c88de-78f0-5e89-9618-54e8fa50e045', 'word_count': 1847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae6c88de-78f0-5e89-9618-54e8fa50e045'}, {'abstract': 'Polar bears have been left stranded on land desperately seeking other things to eat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/20/opinion/the-climate-refugees-of-the-arctic.html', 'snippet': 'Polar bears have been left stranded on land desperately seeking other things to eat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The polar bear, the largest bear of them all and a fearsome predator, is the poster animal of climate change, and for good reason: While most threatened animals, such as the rhinoceros, are victims of localized threats like poaching or human encroachment, the polar bear is threatened most gravely by global emissions of greenhouse gases.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/20/opinion/20tue3web/20tue3web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/20/opinion/20tue3web/20tue3web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/20/opinion/20tue3web/20tue3web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/20/opinion/20tue3web/20tue3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/20/opinion/20tue3web/20tue3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/20/opinion/20tue3web/20tue3web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/20/opinion/20tue3web/20tue3web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Climate Refugees of the Arctic', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Climate Refugees of the Arctic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polar Bears', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kaktovik (Alaska)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-20T08:21:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/45a73479-e4d1-54df-a04a-079a0a8b8c2c', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45a73479-e4d1-54df-a04a-079a0a8b8c2c'}, {'abstract': 'Whether depicting the spectacle of people barreling forward in a snowstorm or the faces of his subjects, mostly black but also white, Adger Cowans’ lyrical images portray life as resonant with feeling.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/12/20/the-heartbeat-of-our-being-in-black-and-white-adger-cowans/', 'snippet': 'Whether depicting the spectacle of people barreling forward in a snowstorm or the faces of his subjects, mostly black but also white, Adger Cowans’ lyrical images portray life as resonant with feeling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The pictures accompanying Adger Cowans’ essay in a new monograph on his work are not his professional photos, but snapshots from his personal life: his childhood home, a group portrait of his mother’s relatives in their Sunday best, and Mr. Cowans cradling his godchild. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Heartbeat of Our Being, in Black and White', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cowans, Adger', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parks, Gordon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kamoinge', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Museum of African American History and Culture', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-20T09:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maurice Berger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maurice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb722e6c-4223-5e9a-a76a-2cbde28302b9', 'word_count': 920, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb722e6c-4223-5e9a-a76a-2cbde28302b9'}, {'abstract': 'The two Texans picked for Trump’s cabinet, Rick Perry and Rex Tillerson, share an instinct for using power and keeping it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/20/opinion/scouts-honor-texas-style.html', 'snippet': 'The two Texans picked for Trump’s cabinet, Rick Perry and Rex Tillerson, share an instinct for using power and keeping it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — Oops! Just when I thought it was safe to come out as a Texan again — you can’t pin Donald J. Trump on us — the president-elect goes and nominates two of my countrymen to his cabinet. And not just any Texans, but two of the most quintessential Texans on the planet: Rick Perry, our former governor, as secretary of energy, and Rex W. Tillerson, the Exxon Mobil chief executive, to head the State Department.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/20/opinion/20swartzWeb/20swartzWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/20/opinion/20swartzWeb/20swartzWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/20/opinion/20swartzWeb/20swartzWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/20/opinion/20swartzWeb/20swartzWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/20/opinion/20swartzWeb/20swartzWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'ima