rt conducts the New York Philharmonic and the Jazz at Lincoln Center Orchestra in the world premiere of Mr. Marsalis’s “The Jungle.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/21/arts/music/a-new-work-from-wynton-marsalis-at-david-geffen-hall.html', 'snippet': 'Alan Gilbert conducts the New York Philharmonic and the Jazz at Lincoln Center Orchestra in the world premiere of Mr. Marsalis’s “The Jungle.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though the week after Christmas is usually a slow period for classical music, the New York Philharmonic has a worthy program. On Wednesday, Dec. 28, Alan Gilbert conducts the combined forces of the Philharmonic and the Jazz at Lincoln Center Orchestra in the world premiere of Wynton Marsalis’s “The Jungle” (Symphony No. 4), a Philharmonic commission. The concert also offers William Bolcom’s Trombone Concerto, a lively, inventive piece that Mr. Gilbert and the orchestra introduced in June; it’s written for Joseph Alessi, the orchestra’s principal trombone, who is again the soloist. The program opens with Copland’s “Quiet City.” (7:30 p.m. Wednesday and Thursday, 8 p.m. Friday, and 7:30 p.m. on Jan. 3; David Geffen Hall, nyphil.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25GUIDE6SUB/25GUIDE6SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25GUIDE6SUB/25GUIDE6SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25GUIDE6SUB/25GUIDE6SUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25GUIDE6SUB/25GUIDE6SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25GUIDE6SUB/25GUIDE6SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25GUIDE6SUB/25GUIDE6SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25GUIDE6SUB/25GUIDE6SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Work From Wynton Marsalis at David Geffen Hall', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Classical; A New Work From Marsalis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jazz at Lincoln Center Orchestra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York String Orchestra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilbert, Alan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marsalis, Wynton', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-21T16:40:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b0dd91f-c137-5f13-a21b-b0e90581c723', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b0dd91f-c137-5f13-a21b-b0e90581c723'}, {'abstract': 'The stars talk about their roles in the new movie and about a circuslike atmosphere on the set.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/21/movies/talking-why-him-with-bryan-cranston-james-franco-and-keegan-michael-key.html', 'snippet': 'The stars talk about their roles in the new movie and about a circuslike atmosphere on the set.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEVERLY HILLS, Calif. — A behind-the-scenes look at the coming comedy “Why Him?” is available on YouTube. The video features a lot of hugging, the smiling faces of the stars Bryan Cranston, James Franco and Keegan-Michael Key, and, often, a happy, playful vibe. When asked if the on-set atmosphere of “Why Him?” ever turned circuslike, Mr. Key, sitting alongside Mr. Franco and Mr. Cranston, paused for a second. “A circus?” he said in a thoughtful, measured tone. “Hmmm. Yes, that’s about right.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25WHY-HIM/25WHY-HIM-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25WHY-HIM/25WHY-HIM-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25WHY-HIM/25WHY-HIM-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25WHY-HIM/25WHY-HIM-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25WHY-HIM/25WHY-HIM-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}},