nventive film series — scores again with “From Coraline to Kubo: The Magic of Laika,” a tribute to the growing Hillsboro, Ore., animation studio. Creatively, Laika has challenged Pixar and DreamWorks Animation with its skilled blending of digital imagery and stop-motion, evident in films like “ParaNorman,” “The Boxtrolls” and, this year, “Kubo and the Two Strings,” which the program offers in 3-D.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25GUIDE3/25GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25GUIDE3/25GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25GUIDE3/25GUIDE3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25GUIDE3/25GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 322, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25GUIDE3/25GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 322}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25GUIDE3/25GUIDE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 549, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25GUIDE3/25GUIDE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1099, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Deep Dive Into Laika’s Animated Worlds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Film; Embracing Laika’s World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMATED FILMS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Laika Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metrograph Theater (Manhattan, NY, Movie Theater)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-21T16:52:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac66eb74-8d76-53e4-9ae9-7ebdc044b92d', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac66eb74-8d76-53e4-9ae9-7ebdc044b92d'}, {'abstract': 'This classic musical, directed by Bartlett Sher, is timely and shines on all fronts. It closes on New Year’s Eve.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/21/theater/fiddler-on-the-roof-revival-has-its-final-notes.html', 'snippet': 'This classic musical, directed by Bartlett Sher, is timely and shines on all fronts. It closes on New Year’s Eve.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Facebook recently, the gifted cabaret singer Liz Callaway posted that she was going to see “Fiddler on the Roof” for the very first time. Friends chimed in, with some registering surprise. (She posted the next day that she adored it.) We all — even critics — have a surprising gap or two in our theatergoing histories. But if you, like Ms. Callaway, are still a “Fiddler” virgin, you have but a week to see the exquisite Broadway revival of this classic musical, directed by Bartlett Sher, which closes on New Year’s Eve.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'cre