et-Zales and Zimmer-Biomet transactions are examples of why not doing a deal is sometimes best.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the most recent merger boom winds down, the broken promises of overeager corporate executives will begin to emerge in earnest. Contrary to the Wall Street spin, one plus one rarely amounts to more than two. The progress of three transactions from the start of the current cycle illustrates the ways investors will be let down in 2017.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sometimes, a Merger Just Doesn’t Pay Off', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Signet Jewelers Ltd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zales Jewelers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zimmer Holdings Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Biomet Incorporated', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hillshire Brands Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tyson Foods Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-21T19:48:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Cox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e5afce4-df92-51ca-848e-43bb3e353561', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e5afce4-df92-51ca-848e-43bb3e353561'}, {'abstract': 'David Zuchowski had led the American unit of the South Korean company for nearly three years, as the U.S. market shifted away from Hyundai’s strengths