 memoir is most direct, and most convincingly self-loathing, about the job of comedy. Many of its details are fiction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In May 2015, Norm Macdonald appeared on the fourth-to-last episode of “Late Show With David Letterman.” He did about six minutes of stand-up comedy, and then choked up when recalling the first time he saw Mr. Letterman perform. Finally, unsuccessfully fighting back tears, he turned toward the host’s desk and told him, “I love you.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/22/arts/22BOOKMACDONALD/22BOOKMACDONALD-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 783, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/22/arts/22BOOKMACDONALD/22BOOKMACDONALD-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 783, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/22/arts/22BOOKMACDONALD/22BOOKMACDONALD-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/22/arts/22BOOKMACDONALD/22BOOKMACDONALD-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/22/arts/22BOOKMACDONALD/22BOOKMACDONALD-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Norm Macdonald’s Often Funny, Always Fabulist ‘Based on a True Story’', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Comedian’s Embroidered Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': 