lusive.html', 'snippet': 'The ride-hailing giant expected to lose money this year, but economic theory suggests it’s handing its passengers a lot of value.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Will Uber Technologies ever make money? The ride-share giant’s recent exit from the cutthroat Chinese market should help, but it may still lose $2.8 billion in earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization, or Ebitda, this year, according to figures reported by The Information on Monday. Economic theory suggests Uber is handing its passengers lots of value. Turning a profit for investors, though, is a different story.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uber’s Value to Riders Is Clear. To Investors, It May Prove More Elusive.', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Uber Technologies Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Car Services and Livery Cabs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kalanick, Travis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-22T19:36:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Beales', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beales', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c7b7b91-1175-5090-85ae-abdd4d8d8263', 'word_count': 927, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c7b7b91-1175-5090-85ae-abdd4d8d8263'}, {'abstract': 'Known for ingenious adaptations of ballet classics, Matthew Bourne tackles perhaps the most famous ballet film of all for his latest work in London.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/22/arts/dance/the-red-shoes-takes-the-stage.html', 'snippet': 'Known for ingenious adaptations of ballet classics, Matthew Bourne tackles perhaps the most famous ballet film of all for his latest work in London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — “Why do you want to dance?” the lordly impresario Boris Lermontov asks the young, beautiful dancer Victoria Page. “Why do you want to live?” she pipes back courageously. These are perhaps the most famous lines in perhaps the most famous ballet film of all: Michael Powell and Emeric Pressburger’s 1948 “The Red Shoes,” a tale about the burning need to dance, the obsessive drive to create art and a heroine who is ultimately driven mad by those demands.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25REDSHOES1/25REDSHOES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25REDSHOES1/25REDSHOES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25REDSHOES1/25REDSHOES1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25REDSHOES1/25REDSHOES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25REDSHOES1/25REDSHOES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/arts/25REDSHOES1/25REDSHOES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'ju