akes us through three old-school musicals that seem to get a tip of the hat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/22/watching/la-la-land-musical-dance-scenes-inspired.html', 'snippet': 'Just about every dance scene in Damien Chazelle’s new movie makes a classic film reference. Monica Castillo takes us through three old-school musicals that seem to get a tip of the hat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s no secret that “La La Land,” the new movie from director Damien Chazelle (“Whiplash”) is a tribute to the flashy musicals of yesteryear. But the film is set in the present, following Mia, a would-be actress (Emma Stone) and Seb, an ambitious jazz musician (Ryan Gosling), both of whom are struggling to achieve their dreams in Los Angeles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/19/arts/la-la-land-watching/la-la-land-watching-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/19/arts/la-la-land-watching/la-la-land-watching-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/19/arts/la-la-land-watching/la-la-land-watching-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/19/arts/la-la-land-watching/19TORONTO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/19/arts/la-la-land-watching/19TORONTO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 413}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/19/arts/la-la-land-watching