 thriller “Patriots Day” dramatizes the 2013 Boston Marathon bombing. This scene takes place later when the F.B.I. used the Black Falcon warehouse to recreate the crime scene. In an interview in New York, Mr. Berg explained how the F.B.I. helped him in constructing his set similar to the way they did on for the bombing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peter Berg Narrates a Scene From ‘Patriots Day’', 'kicker': 'Anatomy of a Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Patriots Day (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-22T23:08:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/daacda7d-e779-577e-bd4c-1521bb1ea09f', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daacda7d-e779-577e-bd4c-1521bb1ea09f'}, {'abstract': 'The 44-year-old founder of the cosmetics brand, who lives on a leafy NoLIta street, is always looking for inspiration, even on the weekends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/22/nyregion/sunday-routine-poppy-king-lipstick-queen.html', 'snippet': 'The 44-year-old founder of the cosmetics brand, who lives on a leafy NoLIta street, is always looking for inspiration, even on the weekends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the founder of the cosmetics brand Lipstick Queen, Poppy King, 44, is always looking for inspiration, even on the weekends. “There’s not an experience that I have where I’m not potentially looking to spark a lipstick concept,” she said. “I never turn off that lens: I can be in the subway or walking down the street and am still thinking of lipstick ideas.” The entrepreneur, born in Melbourne, Australia, has lived in a one-bedroom apartment on a leafy NoLIta street for the past 14 years.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25ROUTINE1/25ROUTINE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25ROUTINE1/25ROUTINE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25ROUTINE1/25ROUTINE1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25ROUTINE1/25ROUTINE1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25ROUTINE1/25ROUTINE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25ROUTINE1/25ROUTINE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25ROUTINE1/25ROUTINE1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Poppy King, Founder of Lipstick Queen, Spends Her Sundays', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Two-Movie Day, Fueled by Bone Broth', 'na