le/8833725f-2f77-51d9-b409-2c7caebb121c', 'word_count': 521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8833725f-2f77-51d9-b409-2c7caebb121c'}, {'abstract': 'The Book Review’s On Poetry columnist picks his favorite books of the year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/22/books/review/the-best-poetry-of-2016.html', 'snippet': 'The Book Review’s On Poetry columnist picks his favorite books of the year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you think of American poetry over the past year, the question that comes to mind is: Will Donald Trump limit himself to a single inaugural poet? And if so, will that poet be Ted Nugent? And if so, will he do a reading of “Cat Scratch Fever”? And if so, will this cause the seas to rise, the skies to darken, the mountains to tremble and the events of Ragnarok to unfold, with the great wolf Fenris devouring Odin the All-Father and even mighty Thor brought low, after slaying the world-encircling Midgard serpent? And if so, will Trump declare this to have been “Sad!”?', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/22/books/review/22poetry-covers/22poetry-covers-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/22/books/review/22poetry-covers/22poetry-covers-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/22/books/review/22poetry-covers/22poetry-covers-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/22/books/review/22poetry-covers/22poetry-covers-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 215, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/22/books/review/22poetry-covers/22poetry-covers-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 215}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/22/books/review/22poetry-covers/22poetry-covers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 306, 'width': 855, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/22/books/review/22poetry-covers/22poetry-covers-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 306, 'width': 855, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Best Poetry of 2016', 'kicker': 'On Poetry', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Best Poetry of 2016', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-22T23:18:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Orr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Orr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a91a0218-6fe8-565e-8f21-f04a505304a4', 'word_count': 1000, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a91a0218-6fe8-565e-8f21-f04a505304a4'}, {'abstract': 'The soda-shop signage and décor at the Ridgewood, Queens, business, which started in 1934, have remained the same. It’s the food selection that has been updated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/22/nyregion/rudys-bakery-and-cafe-ridgewood-queens.html', 'snippet': 'The soda-shop signage and décor at the Ridgewood, Queens, business, which started in 1934, have remained the same. It’s the food selection that has been updated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even as Ridgewood, Queens, undergoes rapid transformations as one of New York’s neighborhoods du jour, Rudy’s Bakery and Cafe, on Seneca Avenue, remains loyal to its old-school identity. The soda-shop signage and unflashy storefront seem to be working just fine for this 82-year-old business.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25JOINT1/25JOINT1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25JOINT1/25JOINT1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 598}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25JOINT1/25JOINT1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1021, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25JOINT1/25JOINT1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2041, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25JOINT1/25JOINT1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25JOINT1/25JOINT1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25JOINT1/25JOINT1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Rudy’s Bakery and C