7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kieny, Marie-Paule', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-22T23:32:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f17f93c9-30eb-5911-885e-e2dd02b13db6', 'word_count': 1168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f17f93c9-30eb-5911-885e-e2dd02b13db6'}, {'abstract': 'This tree has shown itself to be an urban survivor, even among New York City’s asphalt slabs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/22/nyregion/london-plane-tree.html', 'snippet': 'This tree has shown itself to be an urban survivor, even among New York City’s asphalt slabs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The London plane tree is able to withstand the many assaults of urban life. It is often found squeezed tightly into tree pits surrounded by impermeable asphalt and concrete, making rain absorption difficult. Despite their potential size when fully grown, the trees adapt remarkably to cramped quarters, even while overshadowed by buildings and other structures. Often, they are pruned to within an inch of their lives to fit under phone lines or to avoid streetlights. They survive not only runoff from salted roads but also a consistent barrage of raw fertilizer by neighborhood cats and dogs.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25NATURE/25NATURE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25NATURE/25NATURE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25NATURE/25NATURE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25NATURE/25NATURE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25NATURE/25NATURE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25NATURE/25NATURE-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25NATURE/25NATURE-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'London Plane: A Tree With Gritty Roots', 'kicker': 'N.Y.C. Nature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Survivor in the Cities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trees and Shrubs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parks and Recreation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-22T23:38:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Taft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84e03013-46b2-5fcd-8179-c1a7bb4854c6', 'word_count': 497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84e03013-46b2-5fcd-8179-c1a7bb4854c6'}, {'abstract': 'Nova struck out 52 batters and walked just three after being traded to Pittsburgh by the Yankees. He signed a three-year, $26 million contract, according to multiple reports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/22/sports/ivan-nova-pittsburgh-pirates-3-year-deal.html', 'snippet': 'Nova struck out 52 batters and walked just three after being traded to Pittsburgh by the Yankees. He signed a three-year, $26 million contract, according to multiple reports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the flurry of moves the Yankees made this summer, the last one, which came minutes before the Aug. 1 deadline, seemed the most inconsequential: The team sent Ivan Nova to the Pittsburgh Pirates for two minor leaguers to be named later.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/23/sports/23SCOREBOARD/23SCOREBOARD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/23/sports/23SCOREBOARD/23SCOREBOARD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/23/sports/23SCOREBOARD/23SCOREBOARD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/23/sports/23SCOREBOARD/23SCOREBOARD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1639, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/23/sports/23SCOREBOARD/23SCOREBOARD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/23/sports/23SCOREBOARD/23SCOREBOARD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/23/sports/23SCOREBOARD/23SCOREBOARD-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ivan Nova Is Said to Agree to 3-Year Deal to Stay With Pirates', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nova Is Said to Be Staying in Pittsburgh', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Witz, Billy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Free Agents (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Pirates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nova, Ivan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-22T23:43:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Billy Witz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Billy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82fbaac2-6d08-50d9-94a5-2b14c6524672', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82fbaac2-6d08-50d9-94a5-2b14c6524672'}, {'abstract': 'It is hard to know when or how much to get exercised over culinary cultural appropriation when it is class, rather than identity posturing, that is really at issue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/22/nyregion/chopped-cheese-ginia-bellafante.html', 'snippet': 'It is hard to know when or how much to get exercised over culinary cultural appropriation when it is class, rather than identity posturing, that is really at issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Were we to review the year in terms of gastronomic controversies, we might begin and end with the debate over chopped cheese. If your life in New York is purposely dull and cloistered, confined to the Caviar meal-delivery service, Showtime and the obsessive monitoring of Brooklyn real estate listings, then the furor over the sandwich — alternately known as chopped or chop cheese — may have escaped your notice entirely. If that is the case, you are, in effect, part of the problem, as disconnected as the reporter who ventured uptown and “discovered” the sandwich, a longtime offering at bodegas in the Bronx and Harlem, with the surprise of someone coming upon a new moon near Uranus.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25BIG/25BIG-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25BIG/25BIG-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25BIG/25BIG-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25BIG/25BIG-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/25/nyregion/25BIG/25BIG-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 60