od and suggest recipes. That email also appears here. To receive it in your inbox, register here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/20/dining/20COOKING-CINNAMONROLLS1/20COOKING-CINNAMONROLLS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/20/dining/20COOKING-CINNAMONROLLS1/20COOKING-CINNAMONROLLS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/20/dining/20COOKING-CINNAMONROLLS1/20COOKING-CINNAMONROLLS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/20/dining/20COOKING-CINNAMONROLLS1/20COOKING-CINNAMONROLLS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/20/dining/20COOKING-CINNAMONROLLS1/20COOKING-CINNAMONROLLS1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/20/dining/20COOKING-CINNAMONROLLS1/20COOKING-CINNAMONROLLS1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/20/dining/20COOKING-CINNAMONROLLS1/20COOKING-CINNAMONROLLS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Cook This Weekend', 'kicker': 'What to Cook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-23T16:10:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd205d1d-8a21-5ab9-a03a-8562941eff81', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd205d1d-8a21-5ab9-a03a-8562941eff81'}, {'abstract': 'In response to reader concerns, Janet Evanovich has toned down the swearing in some of her books — but not the Stephanie Plum series. “Turbo Twenty-Three,” the latest, is No. 9 in hardcover fiction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/23/books/review/the-story-behind-this-weeks-best-sellers.html', 'snippet': 'In response to reader concerns, Janet Evanovich has toned down the swearing in some of her books — but not the Stephanie Plum series. “Turbo Twenty-Three,” the latest, is No. 9 in hardcover fiction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Criminy: “Turbo Twenty-Three,” the latest entry in Janet Evanovich’s long-running series about the New Jersey bounty hunter Stephanie Plum, is No.\u202f9 in its fifth week on the hardcover fiction list. Evanovich keeps herself busy, James Patterson style: Besides the salty Plum novels, which she writes on her own, she also hit the hardcover list in 2016 with two thrillers she co-wrote — “The Pursuit,” written with Lee Goldberg as part of the Fox and O’Hare series, and “Curious Minds,” written with Phoef Sutton as the debut of the Knight and Moon series. All three share Evanovich’s boisterous humor, but one thing separating the protagonists is their vocabulary, as the website MyCentralJersey.com observed in an interview last summer: “Your newest heroine, Riley Moon, despite two professional degrees from Harvard, never swears,” the reporter Tricia Vanderhoof pointed out. (You have to love that “despite.”) “Instead she says Crikes, Holy Moly, Crikey. .\u2008.\u2008. Why this quirk?”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/23/books/review/23evanovich/23evanovich-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/23/books/review/23evanovich/23evanovich-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/23/books/review/23evanovich/23evanovich-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/23/books/review/23evanovich/23evanovich-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 266, 'width': 260, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/23/books/review/23evanovich/23evanovich-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 266, 'width': 260, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Story Behind This Week’s Best Sellers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside the List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Evanovich, Janet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-23T16:10:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gregory Cowles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/267298f0-0a9b-5f3b-908d-b941c309aea6', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/267298f0-0a9b-5f3b-908d-b941c309aea6'}, {'abstract': 'Humble ingredients, like bright golden beets, can be just as celebratory as caviar and truffles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/23/dining/caviar-beet-salad-smoked-trout-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'Humble ingredients, like bright golden beets, can be just as celebratory as caviar and truffles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For eons, the high-end solution for New Year’s Eve entertaining has been to offer an assortment of fabulous comestibles — Champagne, caviar, smoked salmon, truffles. Like diamonds, these luxury goods never go out of style.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28KITCH1/28KITCH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28KITCH1/28KITCH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28KITCH1/28KITCH1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28KITCH1/28KITCH1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/