States said there would be a cost of imposing “no cost” on the combatants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNITED NATIONS — The United States failed on Friday to gain the votes in the United Nations needed to impose targeted sanctions and an arms embargo on South Sudan, the world’s newest country, which has plunged into an ethnic conflict in which officials from the world body warn of the risks of genocide.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Push for South Sudan Arms Embargo Falls Short at U.N.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Push for Arms Embargo on South Sudan Falls Short', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-23T16:38:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7af04942-a6aa-5c3d-b14c-dc1bd6afa020', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7af04942-a6aa-5c3d-b14c-dc1bd6afa020'}, {'abstract': 'Those Christmas cookies aren’t going to eat themselves. Settle in with a plate, and let the warm glow of cable TV light your way through the aftermath, with offerings ranging from kids movies to classic Westerns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/23/watching/christmas-movie-marathon-cable.html', 'snippet': 'Those Christmas cookies aren’t going to eat themselves. Settle in with a plate, and let the warm glow of cable TV light your way through the aftermath, with offerings ranging from kids movies to classic Westerns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The presents have been opened and the ripped-up wrapping paper is off the floor. Maybe there’s been a little gingerbread and adult-flavored eggnog involved — maybe more than a little. Now what? Let cable TV do the entertaining with several holiday movie marathons over Christmas weekend, including a 24-hour marathon of “A Christmas Story” on TNT and TBS, starting at 8 p.m. on Christmas Eve.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/23/watching/23watching04/23watching04-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/23/watching/23watching04/23watching04-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/23/watching/23watching04/23watching04-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/23/watching/23watching04/23watching04-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/23/watching/23watching04/23watching04-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/23/watching/23watching04/23watching04-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':