578f829', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/004dd540-0af5-5bea-8989-24c50578f829'}, {'abstract': 'Shawn Harrington, who was in the 1994 movie “Hoop Dreams” and became a high school coach, has lost the use of his legs because of a 2014 shooting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/23/sports/ncaabasketball/hoop-dreams-shawn-harrington-guns-chicago.html', 'snippet': 'Shawn Harrington, who was in the 1994 movie “Hoop Dreams” and became a high school coach, has lost the use of his legs because of a 2014 shooting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — The first truly great American sports documentary, it’s universally agreed, was “Hoop Dreams.” Released in 1994, it garnered immediate critical acclaim; Roger Ebert later called it the best film of the decade and “one of the great moviegoing experiences of my lifetime.” Its failure to be nominated for an Academy Award caused such an outcry that the process for nominating Oscar-worthy documentaries was eventually revamped.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/24/sports/24NOCERA1/24NOCERA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/24/sports/24NOCERA1/24NOCERA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/24/sports/24NOCERA1/24NOCERA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/24/sports/24NOCERA1/24NOCERA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1389, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '