 News of the Year', 'kicker': 'Insider Podcasts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights Movement (1954-68)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bowie, David', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cash, Rosanne', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cole, Natalie', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lamar, Kendrick', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prince (1958- )', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simpson, Sturgill', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electoral College', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-27T15:40:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Insider', 'section_name': 'Times Insider', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd0e6ef3-dcd8-52a0-82da-a28339778043', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd0e6ef3-dcd8-52a0-82da-a28339778043'}, {'abstract': 'The panzerotto, a Southern Italian turnover, is the star of a new shop on Macdougal Street.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/27/dining/mr-panzerotto-panzerotti.html', 'snippet': 'The panzerotto, a Southern Italian turnover, is the star of a new shop on Macdougal Street.', 'lead_paragraph': '“New York has every kind of food, but no place that sells panzerotti,” said Christian Francone, who has filled the gap with a sliver of a shop selling the Southern Italian turnovers. “They’re very popular in Italy.” His family is originally from Barletta, in Apulia, home of the fried half-moon snack his shop offers. Twelve fillings are available, including three sweet choices; the savory options, especially those with tomato and mozzarella with or without sausage or pepperoni, taste something like fried pizza. Smoked chicken with pesto and mozzarella, and spinach with ricotta offer a nice change of pace. For now he makes only 100 per day and closes the shop once they are sold. But soon he expects to stay open as late as 3 a.m. on weekends: Mr. Panzerotto, 124 Macdougal Street (Minetta Lane), 646-964-5035, mrpanzerotto.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28BURNER-PANZEROTTI/28BURNER-PANZEROTTI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28BURNER-PANZEROTTI/28BURNER-PANZEROTTI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28BURNER-PANZEROTTI/28BURNER-PANZEROTTI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28BURNER-PANZEROTTI/28BURNER-PANZEROTTI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28BURNER-PANZEROTTI/28BURNER-PANZEROTTI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28BURNER-PANZEROTTI/28BURNER-PANZEROTTI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28BURNER-PANZEROTTI/28BURNER-PANZEROTTI-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Calzone’s Cousin Comes to Greenwich Village', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Discover: Heads Up, New York: Panzerotti Are Here', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mr Panzerotto (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-27T15:40:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e8e543f-9e97-5e96-afc4-85a578d1876f', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e8e543f-9e97-5e96-afc4-85a578d1876f'}, {'abstract': 'Place mats from the Museum of Modern Art are ready for drips from messy eaters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/27/dining/jackson-pollock-placemats-moma.html', 'snippet': 'Place mats from the Museum of Modern Art are ready for drips from messy eaters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Messy eaters? Not a problem when the table is set with these vinyl place mats in a dense Jackson Pollock pattern from the Museum of Modern Art. No drip will show. The only question is, what took the museum so long to come up with the idea? There is also a handsome table runner, 14 by 60 inches, with swaths of white, gray and black on a taupe ground. They’re based on Pollock’s “Number 1A, 1948” and “Number 7, 1950”: Jackson Pollock place mats, $24, table runner $65, momastore.org.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28BURNER-PLACEMAT/28BURNER-PLACEMAT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28BURNER-PLACEMAT/28BURNER-PLACEMAT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28BURNER-PLACEMAT/28BURNER-PLACEMAT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28BURNER-PLACEMAT/28BURNER-PLACEMAT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 479, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28BURNER-PLACEMAT/28BURNER-PLACEMAT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 479}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28BURNER-PLACEMAT/28BURNER-PLACEMAT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 818, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28BURNER-PLACEMAT/28BURNER-PLACEMAT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1635, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Splatter Away With These Pollock Place Mats', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Display: Artist’s Secret: Drips Are Good', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pollock, Jackson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tableware', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-27T15:47:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae9b3924-6e39-548d-a09c-f1b0a8a80cb6', 'word_count': 89, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae9b3924-6e39-548d-a09c-f1b0a8a80cb6'}, {'abstract': 'When Abdou Travare’s wife, Ramata, learned she had dementia, he quit his job to be by her side. His savings have dwindled, and he has struggled to pay the rent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/27/nyregion/neediest-cases-fund-mali-and-senegal.html', 'snippet': 'When Abdou Travare’s wife, Ramata, learned she had dementia, he quit his job to be by her side. His savings have dwindled, and he has struggled to pay the rent.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Don’t scratch it.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/nyregion/28neediesttravare/28neediesttravare-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/28/nyregion/28neediesttravare/28neediesttravare-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/nyregion/28neediesttravare/28neediesttravare-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/nyregion/28neediesttravare/28neediesttravare-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/nyregion/28neediesttravare/28neediesttravare-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/28/nyregion/28neediesttravare/28neediesttravare-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/nyregion/28neediesttravare/28neediesttravare-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giving Up ‘Mostly Everything’ to Care for His Wife', 'kicker': 'The Neediest Cases', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Giving Up Almost Everything to Care for His Wife? ‘I See It as a Pleasure’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Otis, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Catholic Charities Archdiocese of New York', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mali', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Senegal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-27T16:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Otis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52e466bb-544e-54e5-9c60-9e440f5f9ecb', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52e466bb-544e-54e5-9c60-9e440f5f9ecb'}, {'abstract': 'Not as simple as you might think.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/12/27/tariffs-and-the-trade-balance-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'Not as simple as you might think.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before the election, I wrote that I intended to spend the time after in an orgy of serious policy analysis – because I thought we were going to have a president serious about policy. Sad! And in some ways it’s hard to stay motivated about economic analysis when we’re in fact going to have a government that is completely uninterested in analysis, evidence, or truth of any kind.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tariffs and the Trade Balance (Wonkish) (Updated)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-12-27T16:08:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/952c5704-6fa5-513e-8292-b8a9e605475f', 'word_count': 961, 'uri': 'nyt://article/952c5704-6fa5-513e-8292-b8a9e605475f'}, {'abstract': 'The trial of two Englishmen on charges of espionage at Saint Etienne.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/12/27/1891-two-englishmen-found-guilty-on-charges-of-espionage/', 'snippet': 'The trial of two Englishmen on charges of espionage at Saint Etienne.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAINT ETIENNE — John Samuel Cooper and Walter Bednell, the alleged English spies, were brought up for trial before the St. Etienne police magistrates yesterday. The court was crowded, the case having touched a very sensible chord of the French national character.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1891: Two Englishmen Found Guilty on Charges of Espionage', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Saint Etienne', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-27T16:10:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b4c313b-024f-5013-bdfa-95fa25cfcad0', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b4c313b-024f-5013-bdfa-95fa25cfcad0'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Bossert, who was President George W. Bush’s deputy homeland security adviser, will become assistant to the president for homeland security and counterterrorism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/27/us/politics/thomas-bossert-national-security-trump.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Bossert, who was President George W. Bush’s deputy homeland security adviser, will become assistant to the president for homeland security and counterterrorism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEST PALM BEACH, Fla. — President-elect Donald J. Trump has named Thomas P. Bossert, a top national security aide under President George W. Bush, to be his homeland security adviser, the Trump transition team announced Tuesday morning.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/us/28bossert1/28bossert1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/28/us/28bossert1/28bossert1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/us/28bossert1/28bossert1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/us/28bossert1/28bossert1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/28/us/28bossert1/28bossert1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/us/28bossert1/28bossert1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/us/28bossert1/28bossert1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Picks Thomas Bossert as Top Counterterrorism Adviser', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-Bush Adviser Named to a Top Security Post', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bossert, Thomas P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-27T16:10:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22f47876-4132-5800-adc7-c8cbfc11abea', 'word_count': 874, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22f47876-4132-5800-adc7-c8cbfc11abea'}, {'abstract': 'K & M chocolates are a partnership between the chef Thomas Keller and the olive oil producer Armando Manni.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/27/dining/k-plus-m-chocolate-olive-oil.html', 'snippet': 'K & M chocolates are a partnership between the chef Thomas Keller and the olive oil producer Armando Manni.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chef and restaurateur Thomas Keller is now in the chocolate business: a bean-to-bar partnership with Armando Manni, a Tuscan olive oil producer. The idea was born five years ago, when the men were discussing the antioxidant properties of dark chocolate and olive oil. The results, called K & M Extravirgin Chocolate (they say it “K plus M”), are made in a former warehouse in Napa, Calif., where the cacao undergoes a special, gentler process to preserve the bean’s antioxidant properties. Mr. Manni’s olive oil is used in place of cocoa butter. The 75 percent cacao bars come in three varieties, according to the source of the chocolate. The Peruvian bar has coffeelike depth, the bar from Ecuador is smooth with woodsy hints of chestnut, and the Madagascar bar is spicy with notes of pineapple and passion fruit. You do not taste the olive oil: K & M Extravirgin Chocolate, $14.95 for 2.5 ounces at Williams-Sonoma stores, williams-sonoma.com, $120 for eight bars from kellermannichocolate.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28BURNER-CHOCOLATE/28BURNER-CHOCOLATE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28BURNER-CHOCOLATE/28BURNER-CHOCOLATE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28BURNER-CHOCOLATE/28BURNER-CHOCOLATE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28BURNER-CHOCOLATE/28BURNER-CHOCOLATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28BURNER-CHOCOLATE/28BURNER-CHOCOLATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28BURNER-CHOCOLATE/28BURNER-CHOCOLATE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/dining/28BURNER-CHOCOLATE/28BURNER-CHOCOLATE-superJum