, Interrupted', 'kicker': 'Metropolitan Diary', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grand Central Terminal (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-28T01:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eliana Shatkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eliana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shatkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d60cf727-f31a-5c51-9bbd-ade7164578a2', 'word_count': 51, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d60cf727-f31a-5c51-9bbd-ade7164578a2'}, {'abstract': 'The game — a predecessor to Saturday’s College Football Playoff semifinal between No. 1 Alabama and No. 4 Washington — put teams from the South on the map.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/27/sports/ncaafootball/alabama-crimson-tide-washington-huskies.html', 'snippet': 'The game — a predecessor to Saturday’s College Football Playoff semifinal between No. 1 Alabama and No. 4 Washington — put teams from the South on the map.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first time Alabama played Washington, in the 1926 Rose Bowl, the Crimson Tide arrived in Pasadena, Calif., more than a week early. The Huskies, by contrast, did not come down from Seattle until the day before the game, because their officials had determined, according to a New York Times article from Dec. 26, 1925, that “experience has proved that the Huskies play better when they have not been exposed to the enervating Southern breezes for any length of time.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/sports/28colleges1/28colleges1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/28/sports/28colleges1/28colleges1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/sports/28colleges1/28colleges1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/sports/28colleges1/28colleges1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 139, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/28/sports/28colleges1/28colleges1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 139}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/sports/28colleges1/28colleges1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 237, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/sports/28colleges1/28colleges1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 473, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alabama Win in 1926 Rose Bowl Put Southern Stamp on College Football', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Awakening of Southern Football', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tracy, Marc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rose Bowl (Football Game)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Alabama', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Southern States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Football Playoff National Championship', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Washington', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-28T01:02:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Tracy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tracy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ff6cee1-f66f-5a68-980c-38f4819f2bc9', 'word_count': 1110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ff6cee1-f66f-5a68-980c-38f4819f2bc9'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Tapp seemed very much at home in the rural setting of “Hee Haw,” which was taped in Nashville, but he was from Canada.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/27/arts/television/gordie-tapp-hee-haw-regular-of-pfft-you-was-gone-fame-dies-at-94.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Tapp seemed very much at home in the rural setting of “Hee Haw,” which was taped in Nashville, but he was from Canada.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gordie Tapp, a regular for more than 20 years on the long-running television variety series “Hee Haw,” died on Dec. 18 in Burlington, Ontario. He was 94.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/arts/28tapp-obit/28tapp-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/28/arts/28tapp-obit/28tapp-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/28/arts/28tapp-obit/28tapp-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024,