Chance the Rapper', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-28T22:25:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32f749e9-0382-5f45-87ff-11b8f480b36f', 'word_count': 1008, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32f749e9-0382-5f45-87ff-11b8f480b36f'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Matsoukas had a banner 2016, directing Beyoncé’s Grammy-nominated video, “Formation,” and also directing episodes of Issa Rae’s HBO comedy, “Insecure.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/28/arts/music/melina-matsoukas-beyonce-formation-interview.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Matsoukas had a banner 2016, directing Beyoncé’s Grammy-nominated video, “Formation,” and also directing episodes of Issa Rae’s HBO comedy, “Insecure.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'We take music videos for granted. In about 35 years, they’ve gone from an alleged scourge on the musical imagination to a form of oxygen. Every so often, one comes along that touches a nerve or causes a scandal. Back in February, on the eve of the Super Bowl, “Formation” stopped the nation. It was another Beyoncé sneak attack, but also a statement piece and a work of art. And for a month, the intent of its imagery — Beyoncé atop a sinking New Orleans Police Department cruiser; the witchiness of her wide-brimmed hat and her seemingly spiritually possessed head bob on the porch of a manse; a young black boy dancing before a phalanx of militarized cops — was deconstructed, debated and defended.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/29/arts/29MELINA/29MELINA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/29/arts/29MELINA/29MELINA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/29/arts/29MELINA/29MELINA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/29/arts/29MELINA/29MELINA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1463, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/29/arts/29MELINA/29MELINA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/29/arts/29MELINA/29MELINA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/29/arts/29MELINA/29MELINA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Melina Matsoukas Touched Nerves From Behind the Camera', 'kicker': 'The Year in Pop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Melina Matsoukas Touched Nerves From Behind the Camera', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morris, Wesley', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matsoukas, Melina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Formation (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knowles, Beyonce', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rae, Issa', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-28T22:27:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wesley Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wesley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de518a06-f693-523f-adaa-243c363fa2c4', 'word_count': 905, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de518a06-f693-523f-adaa-243c363fa2c4'}, {'abstract': 'With the suite “America’s National Parks” and “A Cosmic Rhythm With Each Stroke,” with the pianist Vijay Iyer, the jazz trumpeter enlightened minds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/28/arts/music/wadada-leo-smith-protest-music-interview.html', 'snippet': 'With the suite “America’s National Parks” and “A Cosmic Rhythm With Each Stroke,” with the pianist Vijay Iyer, the jazz trumpeter enlightened minds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The trumpeter and composer Wadada Leo Smith made not one but two of this year’s standout jazz releases. “America’s National Parks,” a suite on two discs, features his Golden Quintet, made up of longtime associates like the pianist Anthony Davis and the drummer Pheeroan akLaff. “A Cosmic Rhythm With Each Stroke” is a duo session with another colleague, the pianist Vijay Iyer, inspired by the art of the Indian modernist Nasreen Mohamedi.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/29/arts/29WADDA/29WADDA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/29/arts/29WADDA/29WADDA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlarg