ality the key to being a good person?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/roomfordebate/2016/12/29/does-empathy-guide-or-hinder-moral-action', 'snippet': 'Is empathy or rationality the key to being a good person?', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/27/opinion/RFD-empathy/RFD-empathy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/27/opinion/RFD-empathy/RFD-empathy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/27/opinion/RFD-empathy/RFD-empathy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/27/opinion/RFD-empathy/RFD-empathy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/27/opinion/RFD-empathy/RFD-empathy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/27/opinion/RFD-empathy/RFD-empathy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/27/opinion/RFD-empathy/RFD-empathy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2045, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Does Empathy Guide or Hinder Moral Action?', 'kicker': 'Room for Debate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-12-29T08:57:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52455200-d069-5021-b2f6-4c755cb2ffba', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52455200-d069-5021-b2f6-4c755cb2ffba'}, {'abstract': 'Ioana Moldovan photographed the daily life of a family doctor, who sees medicine as more of a “calling than a career,” in rural southwestern Romania.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/12/29/the-devotion-of-an-old-fashioned-doctor-in-romania/', 'snippet': 'Ioana Moldovan photographed the daily life of a family doctor, who sees medicine as more of a “calling than a career,” in rural southwestern Romania.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a little girl, Ioana Moldovan eagerly awaited her vacations at her grandfather’s house in southwestern Transylvania. He lived in a steel mill town, where he raised rows of tomatoes, cucumbers, strawberries, cranberries and cherries, which Ms. Moldovan would eat directly from the trees. While her grandfather, Ion Ciugudean, did not talk much about his work as a radiologist, he did seem to know everyone in the village. Whenever he would go to the market, shopkeepers and customers would say hello and treat him with the same respect he treated his patients. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Devotion of an Old-Fashioned Doctor in Romania', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rural Areas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moldovan, Ioana', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'or