article/163b3c86-82d0-59e7-beef-a3132835938e'}, {'abstract': 'What is happening with Kanye West? We spend this week’s episode of Still Processing discussing that question.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/29/podcasts/we-need-to-talk-about-kanye.html', 'snippet': 'What is happening with Kanye West? We spend this week’s episode of Still Processing discussing that question.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year has been especially heavy with untimely popular culture deaths. In the past week, George Michael and Carrie Fisher joined that tally. Neither was entirely comfortable with fame, even though Ms. Fisher, as the daughter of Debbie Reynolds and Eddie Fisher, was born with fame virtually in her bloodstream. Her ambivalence always seemed healthy even when she herself was not. Their deaths are an occasion to think about the toll fame takes on a person, not only on the dead but also on the living. What if that person is Kanye West?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/29/arts/29PROCESSING/29PROCESSING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/29/arts/29PROCESSING/29PROCESSING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/29/arts/29PROCESSING/29PROCESSING-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/29/arts/29PROCESSING/29PROCESSING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/29/arts/29PROCESSING/29PROCESSING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight