f engravings and paintings that illustrate what Lower Manhattan looked like in colonial times. But what did it sound like? As St. Paul’s Chapel continues to celebrate the 250th anniversary of its founding, an ambitious music program at Trinity Wall Street conjures sounds from the past as part of its Time’s Arrow festival, which begins Sunday, Jan. 1.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/01/01/arts/01GUIDE8/01GUIDE8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/01/01/arts/01GUIDE8/01GUIDE8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 448}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/01/01/arts/01GUIDE8/01GUIDE8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/01/01/arts/01GUIDE8/01GUIDE8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1531, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/01/01/arts/01GUIDE8/01GUIDE8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/01/01/arts/01GUIDE8/01GUIDE8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/01/01/arts/01GUIDE8/01GUIDE8-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Conjuring Musical and Colonial Ghosts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None,