s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AFROJACK Afrojack has been hovering near the top tier of global D.J.s for a few years now, but he’s never quite connected as an artist on his own terms (like, say, the successful but uninspired Calvin Harris). But this year, he released “Gone,” an extremely temperate and sneakily effective collaboration with Ty Dolla Sign, and maybe there’s more where that came from. At 8 p.m., the Gallery in the Dream Downtown, Manhattan; NYCNewYears.com. (Jon Caramanica)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/30/arts/30newyearspop-disclosure/30newyearspop-disclosure-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/30/arts/30newyearspop-disclosure/30newyearspop-disclosure-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/30/arts/30newyearspop-disclosure/30newyearspop-disclosure-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/30/arts/30newyearspop-disclosure/30newyearspop-disclosure-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/30/arts/30newyearspop-disclosure/30newyearspop-disclosure-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/30/arts/30newyearspop-disclosure/30newyearspop-disclosure-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thum