r discharges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kristofer Goldsmith spent the end of his teenage years photographing mutilated bodies. Mr. Goldsmith knew that he would face bullets and bombs when he enlisted in the Army shortly after Sept. 11, and like almost every soldier of his generation, he volunteered to serve with the understanding that he would go to war. He made sergeant in just over two years and spent an entire year in Baghdad.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/30/opinion/30rowan/30rowan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/30/opinion/30rowan/30rowan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/30/opinion/30rowan/30rowan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/30/opinion/30rowan/30rowan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 447, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/30/opinion/30rowan/30rowan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 447}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/30/opinion/30rowan/30rowan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/30/opinion/30rowan/30rowan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1527, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Less Than Honorable Policy', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Less Than Honorable Policy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amnesties, Commutations and Pardons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vietnam Veterans of America', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldsmith, Kristofer', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-30T08:23:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Rowan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rowan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/af82a24c-7db8-5060-8a85-c31f14cdde5a', 'word_count': 865, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af82a24c-7db8-5060-8a85-c31f14cdde5a'}, {'abstract': 'Another refugee banished by Australia to Manus Island has died, the latest victim of a form of dehumanization that threatens the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/30/opinion/australias-death-by-numbers.html', 'snippet': 'Another refugee banished by Australia to Manus Island has died, the latest victim of a form of dehumanization that threatens the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The dead refugee had a name. But even in death Australia did not want to humanize him. For years now he had been no more than a registration number — BRF063 — under the country’s cruel refugee deterrence system known as “offshore processing.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/31/opinion/31cohen-inyt/31cohen-inyt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 993, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/31/opinion/31cohen-inyt/31cohen-inyt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 993}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/31/opinion/31cohen-inyt/31cohen-inyt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 619, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/31/opinion/31cohen-inyt/31cohen-inyt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1192, 'width': 720, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/31/opinion/31cohen-inyt/31cohen-inyt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/31/opinion/31cohen-inyt/31cohen-inyt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/31/opinion/31cohen-inyt/31cohen-inyt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Australia’s Death by Numbers', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Australia’s death by numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manus Island (Papua New Guinea)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nauru', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-30T09:36:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roger Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roger', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5bf7757-203c-5789-a3e9-bb1369364095', 'word_count': 843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5bf7757-203c-5789-a3e9-bb1369364095'}, {'abstract': 'Make a snow angel to determine size. Punch a small hole near the top for airflow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/30/magazine/how-to-build-an-igloo.html', 'snippet': 'Make a snow angel to determine size. Punch a small hole near the top for airflow.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Make friends with winter,” says Norbert E. Yankielun, an engineer who has written about igloo construction. “Igloos are the most specialized form of a snow shelter, and you need a special type of snow to do it right. The truly appropriate snow is somewhere where there is not a freeze-and-thaw cycle. That kind of weather destroys the structural integrity of the snow.” But even though ideal igloo-making environments are closer to the polar regions, it’s not impossible to replicate good conditions elsewhere.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': No