let stretch limousines cruise without seatbelts and protections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eight young women out on a tour of Long Island wineries had both safety and comfort in mind when they booked a stretch limousine for their pre-wedding celebration in the summer of 2015. But four of them died and two were severely injured when the driver attempted a U-turn on a busy county highway and the long limousine was broadsided in traffic.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/31/opinion/31sat2/31sat2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/31/opinion/31sat2/31sat2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/31/opinion/31sat2/31sat2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/31/opinion/31sat2/31sat2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/31/opinion/31sat2/31sat2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 533}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/31/opinion/31sat2/31sat2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 910, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/31/opinion/31sat2/31sat2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1197, 'width': 1347, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Lethal Allure of Stretch Limos', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Lethal Allure of Stretch Limos', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Car Services and Livery Cabs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-31T00:46:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/84ae9317-f76d-55ee-9b67-a8bf4dd9b828', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84ae9317-f76d-55ee-9b67-a8bf4dd9b828'}, {'abstract': 'There is something about celebrity mothers and daughters like Debbie Reynolds and Carrie Fisher that captures the imagination in a way that famous father-sons do not.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/30/arts/debbie-reynolds-carrie-fisher-relationship.html', 'snippet': 'There is something about celebrity mothers and daughters like Debbie Reynolds and Carrie Fisher that captures the imagination in a way that famous father-sons do not.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For anyone who loves the spotlight, mothering can be an ideal role — for a while. The mother is a singular star to her baby, whose gaze follows her around the room with the watchfulness of an obsessive fan. For the stars Carrie Fisher and Debbie Reynolds, that dynamic seemed to linger well into Ms. Fisher’s childhood: Ms. Fisher was the reverent observer, her mother the adored and observed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debbie Reynolds and Carrie Fisher, a Mother-Daughter Act for the Ages', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In and Out of the Spotlight, a Mother-Daughter Act for the Ages', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fisher, Carrie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reynolds, Debbie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Bright Lights: Starring Carrie Fisher and Debbie Reynolds (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Postcards from the Edge (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-31T00:46:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Dominus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dominus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a019287d-20b8-55e7-9941-744072261039', 'word_count': 1205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a019287d-20b8-55e7-9941-744072261039'}, {'abstract': 'Under international pressure, Moscow still does not admit to the responsibility of the highest levels of government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/30/opinion/russias-contorted-denials-on-doping.html', 'snippet': 'Under international pressure, Moscow still does not admit to the responsibility of the highest levels of government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a moment there it looked as if Russia had finally fessed up about its gigantic sports doping operation, even though a senior official’s acknowledgment of an “institutional conspiracy” in an interview with Rebecca Ruiz of The Times was coupled with the usual whining about how Russia was being pilloried for what everybody does. But then the official, as well as the minister of sports, came back and said the comment was taken out of context. And just like that, the matter was back to square one.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/31/opinion/31sat3web/31sat3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/31/opinion/31sat3web/31sat3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/31/opinion/31sat3web/31sat3web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/31/opinion/31sat3web/31sat3web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1381, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/31/opinion/31sat3web/31sat3web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/12/31/opinion/31sat3web/31sat3web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/31/opinion/31sat3web/31sat3web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia’s Contorted Denials on Doping', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia’s Contorted Denials on Doping', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2014)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodchenkov, Grigory', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Anti-Doping Agency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Steroids', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Antseliovich, Anna', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-12-31T00:51:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/51544a3a-7250-5998-b755-7d1de82d72f6', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51544a3a-7250-5998-b755-7d1de82d72f6'}, {'abstract': 'A century ago, a battalion on its way to the European front played in a league with top players. Though the experiment fizzled, it helped change the sport.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/30/sports/hockey/wwi-canadian-soldiers-national-hockey-association-stanley-cup.html', 'snippet': 'A century ago, a battalion on its way to the European front played in a league with top players. Though the experiment fizzled, it helped change the sport.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Canada, the kinship between hockey and war is implicit. Both (of course) stoke patriotic pride, and there’s the recognition (maybe) that the vivid game that remains closest to the national heart reflects the confusion and desperate violence of the battlefield, while also (somehow) naturally honoring warrior values of bravery and perseverance.', 'pri