the reporters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/30/nyregion/upper-brookville-long-island-new-york-russia.html', 'snippet': 'The vehicles’ occupants, who appeared to be mostly middle-aged men and women, would not lower their windows to speak to the reporters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UPPER BROOKVILLE, N.Y. — Seven miles from here, an old-world mansion known as the Killenworth estate became, briefly, a center of international intrigue on Thursday as reporters began descending on the property, long a weekend retreat for Russian diplomats. President Obama had just announced that he would be closing a “Russian compound” in New York that had been used for intelligence gathering — and several administration officials pointed to Killenworth, which is in Glen Cove, as the target in New York.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/31/nyregion/31OYSTER/31OYSTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/12/31/nyregion/31OYSTER/31OYSTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/31/nyregion/31OYSTER/31OYSTER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/31/nyregion/31OYSTER/31OYSTER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1338, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/12/31/nyregion/31OYSTER/31OYSTER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thu